{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability","id":1047667,"title":"[2E] Should not Sacred Hunt be inner ability?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-12T05:44:08-08:00","id":1047667,"title":"[2E] Should not Sacred Hunt be inner ability?","content":"Siskur-Dah is crucial to 2E games. It's both setting and mechanical center piece of Werewolf. Every Uratha needs to make it and fulfill Hunt, or they start loosing Harmony to Flesh. So I wonder- Why it's not inner ability of Uratha template, but 2 dot Rite? I could also see reasons for making it only 1 for Rite to make every character make one after short trening - but making it 2 dot just don't make sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T05:51:31-08:00","id":1047669,"title":"","content":"I think I heard this somewhere on the forums before. Something about the invoking the Sacred Hunt is well, <i>sacred</i>. It is a willing and conscious act to honor and fulfill one's heritage as scions of the God of the Hunt,<br /> <br /> I compare it to how even if you are born into a culture or the beliefs of a religion, you aren't really &quot;of&quot; that culture/faith without actively practicing its rituals and customs, no matter how much you claim to identify yourself with that group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T07:01:10-08:00","id":1047679,"title":"","content":"It's not an innate ability because originally, they didn't need it. In Pangaea all hunts counted as sacred. When it fell, the werewolves had to come up with an artificial method of inducing the conditions in the flesh and shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T07:05:17-08:00","id":1047682,"title":"","content":"Ohhh, that one too. Totally slipped my mind.<br /> <br /> The fall of Pangaea was a big hit on the werewolf race. Once, they were the dominant species. Now, they've been reduced to hiding amongst their prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T07:36:33-08:00","id":1047695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability#post1047667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Siskur-Dah is crucial to 2E games. It's both setting and mechanical center piece of Werewolf. Every Uratha needs to make it and fulfill Hunt, or they start loosing Harmony to Flesh. So I wonder- Why it's not inner ability of Uratha template, but 2 dot Rite? I could also see reasons for making it only 1 for Rite to make every character make one after short trening - but making it 2 dot just don't make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sacred Hunt is a 2-dot Rite and werewolves get 2 free dots of Rites as a base template ability. Doing it this way simply allows for more flexibility, so if your pack already has someone with your Tribe's version of Sacred Hunt, you can use those two dots on Chain Rage or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T08:21:20-08:00","id":1047710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047695#post1047695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sacred Hunt is a 2-dot Rite and werewolves get 2 free dots of Rites as a base template ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, I missed that - I was totally convinced it was 1 dot of Rites at character creation. Still, Sacred Hunt as 2 dot Rite seems rather costly to it's usability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-12-2017, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T09:23:04-08:00","id":1047731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047669#post1047669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I heard this somewhere on the forums before. Something about the invoking the Sacred Hunt is well, <i>sacred</i>. It is a willing and conscious act to honor and fulfill one's heritage as scions of the God of the Hunt,<br /> <br /> I compare it to how even if you are born into a culture or the beliefs of a religion, you aren't really &quot;of&quot; that culture/faith without actively practicing its rituals and customs, no matter how much you claim to identify yourself with that group.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been a thing of much contention for certain present parties when the game first came out. And the sacredness of it being re-affirmed as a rite is definitely a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T10:35:25-08:00","id":1047768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047679#post1047679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not an innate ability because originally, they didn't need it. In Pangaea all hunts counted as sacred. When it fell, the werewolves had to come up with an artificial method of inducing the conditions in the flesh and shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. It's because they don't belong in this world. It's also so they have to invest themselves somewhat in the culture or spirituality, either learning it from a werewolf or a spirit, or see what 'not belonging in the world' leads to. The natural ability left them with Pangaea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:25:49-08:00","id":1047811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability#post1047667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Siskur-Dah is crucial to 2E games. It's both setting and mechanical center piece of Werewolf. Every Uratha needs to make it and fulfill Hunt, or they start loosing Harmony to Flesh. So I wonder- Why it's not inner ability of Uratha template, but 2 dot Rite? I could also see reasons for making it only 1 for Rite to make every character make one after short trening - but making it 2 dot just don't make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally i just give it for free when a character joins a tribe because otherwise it feels like a cheap shot when they got to spent 2XP in a rite that otherwise cant really play without.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:34:54-08:00","id":1047816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047811#post1047811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally i just give it for free when a character joins a tribe because otherwise it feels like a cheap shot when they got to spent 2XP in a rite that otherwise cant really play without.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, you get 2XP worth of Rites for free at character creation. If you chose to spend that 2 free XP on something other than the thing you can't play without, that's you making the conscious choice to play that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:48:38-08:00","id":1047824,"title":"","content":"I understands now <i>why </i>Sacred Hunt is needed to be Rite in first place. <b>I still just thinks making it 2 dot one is rather illogical - it's the first Rite every one Uratha would learn, any time.</b> It's still a Rite, but invoked every time pack goes on Hunt - that is, almost every other day. Making it 'very specialized part of what you are you learn after monthes or even year of traning' ( as 2 dot idicate ) does not mesh with in setting material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-12-2017, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:54:11-08:00","id":1047830,"title":"","content":"Not every Uratha would learn it. If you're a part of a pack, it makes more sense for the ritemaster to have it. And it's not invoked almost every day, I don't know where you got that idea, the sacred hunt is a special affair. The only ones who might be invoking it frequently are particularly powerful or religious werewolves, and they would justify learning it themselves.<br /> <br /> But if you're not interested in having rites, those free dots of rites are best used for Sacred Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2017, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:06:39-08:00","id":1047836,"title":"","content":"Nooooo... EVERY Uratha should have Sacred Hunt because it let's them stop Harmony Breaking Points and Essence bleed. If you are just a bit longer without your pack - and not every Uratha have pack, this very moment - they will need to commerce it themselves. I do not see reasons <i>why</i> you would not learn it as every single characters first one Rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:10:44-08:00","id":1047837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047836#post1047836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nooooo... EVERY Uratha should have Sacred Hunt because it let's them stop Harmony Breaking Points and Essence bleed.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're part of a pack, and one member has the rite, that's not much of a concern. One member performs the rite for the whole pack every couple months and you're set.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you are just a bit longer without your pack - and not every Uratha have pack, this very moment - they will need to commerce it themselves. </div> </div> </div>This is why it pays to be part of a pack and not a lone wolf. But even if you are a lone wolf, provided you've met another Uratha or dealt with spirits, you can learn this rite on your own and use it on your own. If you don't, that's a risk you choose to pay. If you did automatically learn it, no werewolf would need to be part of werewolf society, there would be no recognizable consequences of the loss of Pangaea, and no one would ever suffer a Breaking Point or Essence bleed from not hunting. There would be no reason to hunt at all and the idea of it being 'sacred' would be thrown out the window.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not see reasons <i>why</i> you would not learn it as every single characters first one. </div> </div> </div>Because if you're making a pack of werewolves and one person chooses to get Sacred Hunt, no one else has to and they can get whatever they want. There's no point in every member of the pack having it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:23:39-08:00","id":1047846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047824#post1047824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understands now <i>why </i>Sacred Hunt is needed to be Rite in first place. <b>I still just thinks making it 2 dot one is rather illogical - it's the first Rite every one Uratha would learn, any time.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. One use of the Rite covers the whole pack, so each pack only needs one person who knows it (probably the pack's dedicated ritemaster). If you have a multi-tribal pack, you might want one member of each represented Tribe to know it so you can get their specific Tribe benefits, but you don't need every single member to know it. As a new Uratha, you would probably train under an existing pack until you're ready to start your own, and that pack will certainly have at least one ritemaster who can perform the Sacred Hunt, so it doesn't make sense to teach it to you right away. It might be something taught to you as a right of passage, when you're ready to lead your first hunt, and then only if you expressesed interest and/or showed promise in that skill. Someone who was especially skilled with spirits might be taught Bottle Spirit instead, or Totemic Empowerment and Banish. Someone who showed great reverence for their territory might be taught Hunting Ground first. There's no reason every Uratha would need to know Sacred Hunt - the whole point of working in a pack is to combine your strengths and cover each other's weaknesses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047824#post1047824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still a Rite, but invoked every time pack goes on Hunt - that is, almost every other day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not quite that often, especially since some hunts will last more than a day. But even if you assume you're doing it that often, you still only need one person out of like five to know it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047824#post1047824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making it 'very specialized part of what you are you learn after monthes or even year of traning' ( as 2 dot idicate ) does not mesh with in setting material.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way does a 2-dot Rite represent a very specialized skill you would learn after months or years of training?? That sounds extremely excessive. Heck, everyone gets 2 dots of Rites for free, which tells me a 2 dot Rite is the kind of training most Uratha are expected to have as a baseline before striking it out on their own. Not to mention you can trade in up to 5 of your Merit dots for Rite dots at character creation, so even 7 dots, while highly specialized, is within the scope of a new Uratha's basic training.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-12-2017, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:27:54-08:00","id":1047849,"title":"","content":"Bottle spirit is one of the limited ones, only taught to Bone Shadows. Though it would make sense for them to be considered especially skilled with spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:29:37-08:00","id":1047851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047849#post1047849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bottle spirit is one of the limited ones, only taught to Bone Shadows. Though it would make sense for them to be considered especially skilled with spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why I added &quot;or Totemic Empowerment and Banish.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:35:16-08:00","id":1047860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047837#post1047837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're part of a pack, and one member has the rite, that's not much of a concern. One member performs the rite for the whole pack every couple months and you're set.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why it's overrated right now. It should be 'mass Rite' in Uratha population, how it's constructed by setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047837#post1047837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why it pays to be part of a pack and not a lone wolf. But even if you are a lone wolf, provided you've met another Uratha or dealt with spirits, you can learn this rite on your own and use it on your own. If you don't, that's a risk you choose to pay.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>If any local Tribes or Protectorate thinks straight, they will not agree with you on this - because Harmony is making you in check with Death Rage, giving tools to maintaining it it should be <i>first thing you teach to new </i>Uratha, with packs or not.</b> Stoping Harmony automatic Breaking Points Rite seems like this kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Also,<b> being without pack maybe not your own choice</b> - Uratha leads violent lives, many times in books are described ones that lost their old packs and have 'lone survivor' syndrom over them. Not to mentions area when you are only pack in nearby, and suddenly your packmates are dead. So no, sometimes going without Sacred Hunt Rite is not your choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047837#post1047837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you did automatically learn it, no werewolf would need to be part of werewolf society,</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I did mark that I understand why Sacred Hunt should <b>not</b> be learn automatic - only that's it overpriced as 2 dot one.<br /> <br /> Second, I beg to differ on society argument - being part of Tribes, packs and Lodges comes with other bonuses making staying with society worthwhile. Ha, I even go with other gameplay from other <b>CoD</b> game - Does making <i>High Speech</i> Merit free bonus for sticking with Orders in Mage make it more compelling to join them or not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047837#post1047837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">there would be no recognizable consequences of the loss of Pangaea</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally wrong - existing of Gauntlet, dichotomy of Flesh and Spirit, or even simple lack of Wolf with us now are reasons to rise Pangaea again - and by this, why it's loss was a shock. Just read <b>Pure</b> book - there are at least a dozen arguments why to make return of Pangaea thing, from Uratha perspective. It's just very bad idea for humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047837#post1047837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and no one would ever suffer a Breaking Point or Essence bleed from not hunting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <b><i>never</i></b> said there should be change on this part of mechanics. I'm all in for Breaking Points or Essence bleeds - just young pups should start much easier w Sacred Hunt Rite itself, if it is so 'sacred' to being Uratha. If Hunt is like prayer, each character should be able to do this, not only one that choose this common Rite for any other. Virtually <i>all</i> Uratha should be able to commerce Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047837#post1047837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There would be no reason to hunt at all and the idea of it being 'sacred' would be thrown out the window.</div> </div> </div> </div>Invalid part of argument, as you clearly totally missed my point. Hunt is needed in game - it's just weird it's so costly for starting characters to do it themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047837#post1047837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if you're making a pack of werewolves and one person chooses to get Sacred Hunt, no one else has to and they can get whatever they want. There's no point in every member of the pack having it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting as written seems to be different here with you - all it's say that if <i>pack is all good</i>, you do not need Rite. Situation like those are... not often. Not to mention that each Tribe and Lodge have their own Rite's variant, so it's <b><i>beneficial </i></b>for the pack to have multiple Sacred Hunt ritemasters, not only on the reason of 'our Ithaeur is barely living and cannot make us Rite'. I literally have example of this in our game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-12-2017, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T13:54:20-08:00","id":1047870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047816#post1047816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again though, you get 2XP worth of Rites for free at character creation. If you chose to spend that 2 free XP on something other than the thing you can't play without, that's you making the conscious choice to play that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont really use the intended &quot;level&quot; of chargen the game offers as i have mostly people new to the games and intended chargen is overwhelming so its mostly 1 gift, one renown, no tribe and off you go. But when i have use it i have never had anyone not picking the hunt rite. However what i never had in my game is redundant pcs (two of the same tribe/auspice)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:08:24-08:00","id":1047877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047846#post1047846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what way does a 2-dot Rite represent a very specialized skill you would learn after months or years of training?? That sounds extremely excessive. Heck, everyone gets 2 dots of Rites for free, which tells me a 2 dot Rite is the kind of training most Uratha are expected to have as a baseline before striking it out on their own. Not to mention you can trade in up to 5 of your Merit dots for Rite dots at character creation, so even 7 dots, while highly specialized, is within the scope of a new Uratha's basic training.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, as rite dont really a have requirement like Lunar gifts does mean that there no ineherent mastery status to know 5 dots rites. Its just a cost. Even one of the most basic wisdom renown act is making a fetish which is a 4 level rite so there is little relation in a werewolf &quot;badassery&quot; and their rites levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047837#post1047837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you did automatically learn it, no werewolf would need to be part of werewolf society, there would be no recognizable consequences of the loss of Pangaea,</div> </div> </div> </div>Well forsaken 1st edition didnt had the hunt rite or at least not in the same way as it is now and Uratha &quot;society&quot; such as it is was fine and &quot;working&quot;. I have my issues on how contradictory it was but still. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047837#post1047837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you did automatically learn it, no werewolf would need to be part of werewolf society, there would be no recognizable consequences of the loss of Pangaea, and no one would ever suffer a Breaking Point or Essence bleed from not hunting. There would be no reason to hunt at all and the idea of it being 'sacred' would be thrown out the window.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that i doubt werewolf who suffer from breaking points for not hunting do so for just not getting the 2XP worth of a rite. Most likely they are on the whole peter parker plot of &quot;i dont wanna be spiderman anymore and just be regular human.&quot; <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.comicvine.com/uploads/original/12/123644/2867907-2731807__spider_man_no_more.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:09:07-08:00","id":1047878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047870#post1047870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont really use the intended &amp;quot;level&amp;quot; of chargen the game offers as i have mostly people new to the games and intended chargen is overwhelming so its mostly 1 gift, one renown, no tribe and off you go.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the fault of the rules that they don't work right when you change them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047870#post1047870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But when i have use it i have never had anyone not picking the hunt rite. However what i never had in my game is redundant pcs (two of the same tribe/auspice)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a problem there. If everyone is using their two free Rite dots for Sacred Hunt, that's functionally no different that Sacred Hunt coming free at character creation. However, if you'd had two or more characters of the same Tribe in the same pack, they <i>could have</i> used those dots on something else, making it more flexible than if you just got Sacred Hunt for free at character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:27:48-08:00","id":1047888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047860#post1047860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>If any local Tribes or Protectorate thinks straight, they will not agree with you on this - because Harmony is making you in check with Death Rage, giving tools to maintaining it it should be <i>first thing you teach to new </i>Uratha, with packs or not.</b> Stoping Harmony automatic Breaking Points Rite seems like this kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to know Sacred Hunt to prevent Harmony Breaking Points, you just need to participate in Siskur-Dah. The Rite can be performed by someone else. And even if you don't have anyone who can do the Rite for you, you can always compensate by hitting Breaking Points in the opposite direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047860#post1047860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also,<b> being without pack maybe not your own choice</b> - Uratha leads violent lives, many times in books are described ones that lost their old packs and have 'lone survivor' syndrom over them. Not to mentions area when you are only pack in nearby, and suddenly your packmates are dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is a risk you take in choosing not to learn the Sacred Hunt Rite yourself. If you don't find that to be an acceptable risk, take Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047860#post1047860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no, sometimes going without Sacred Hunt Rite is not your choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is always the player's choice not to take the Sacred Hunt Rite with their free Rite dots. If that choice leads to consequences down the line, good. Consequences are what stories are built on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047860#post1047860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I did mark that I understand why Sacred Hunt should <b>not</b> be learn automatic - only that's it overpriced as 2 dot one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like a strange thing to get hung up on, considering the character creation rules give you enough free Rite dots to buy it. I'm sure if it had been a 1 dot Rite, you would only have gotten 1 free Rite dot at character creation, and 2 seems like a reasonable cost for the benefits it gives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047860#post1047860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, I beg to differ on society argument - being part of Tribes, packs and Lodges comes with other bonuses making staying with society worthwhile. Ha, I even go with other gameplay from other <b>CoD</b> game - Does making <i>High Speech</i> Merit free bonus for sticking with Orders in Mage make it more compelling to join them or not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a very good analogy, since you only get High Speech for free if you're in an Order, but you get two dots of Rites for free even if you're a Ghost Wolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047860#post1047860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <b><i>never</i></b> said there should be change on this part of mechanics. I'm all in for Breaking Points or Essence bleeds - just young pups should start much easier w Sacred Hunt Rite itself, if it is so 'sacred' to being Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Nofather was getting at is that if there was no possibility of starting without Sacred Hunt, then the Breaking Points and Essence Bleed for not going on Siskur-Dah would be pretty pointless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047860#post1047860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Hunt is like prayer, each character should be able to do this, not only one that choose this common Rite for any other. Virtually <i>all</i> Uratha should be able to commerce Sacred Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going on Siskur-Dah is prayer. Performing the Sacred Hunt Rite is <i>leading your pack in prayer</i>. Virtually all Uratha <i>do</i> participate in Siskur-Dah, but they don't all lead the Rite, just like not all Christians lead a congregation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047860#post1047860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Invalid part of argument, as you clearly totally missed my point. Hunt is needed in game - it's just weird it's so costly for starting characters to do it themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two experiences is not &quot;so costly&quot;. It's the same price as a single dot in a Skill. And you get it for free at character creation if you want it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047860#post1047860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Setting as written seems to be different here with you - all it's say that if <i>pack is all good</i>, you do not need Rite. Situation like those are... not often. Not to mention that each Tribe and Lodge have their own Rite's variant, so it's <b><i>beneficial </i></b>for the pack to have multiple Sacred Hunt ritemasters, not only on the reason of 'our Ithaeur is barely living and cannot make us Rite'. I literally have example of this in our game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and that's a choice you can make. If your pack doesn't already have a Storm Lord with Sacred Hunt (or whatever), it might be worthwhile for you to spend your free dots on it. Even if they do, it might be a good idea to take it, in case the other Storm Lord gets injured or captured or killed. But it also might be worthwhile to take Hunting Ground or something instead. At the risk of being temporarily without your Tribe's version of Sacred Hunt, you expand your pack's access to other Rites. And if that risk ends up biting you in the ass, that creates drama for the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-12-2017, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:36:14-08:00","id":1047893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047837#post1047837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if you're making a pack of werewolves and one person chooses to get Sacred Hunt, no one else has to and they can get whatever they want. There's no point in every member of the pack having it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats kind of proving Wyrdhamster point, one player at least have to bite the bullet to have this thing that is needed to play the game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047878#post1047878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see a problem there. If everyone is using their two free Rite dots for Sacred Hunt, that's functionally no different that Sacred Hunt coming free at character creation. However, if you'd had two or more characters of the same Tribe in the same pack, they <i>could have</i> used those dots on something else, making it more flexible than if you just got Sacred Hunt for free at character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because its a lie of a choice, is giving then the choice but then there is only 1 option that is not gonna cripple them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T14:55:36-08:00","id":1047907,"title":"","content":"Learning Sacred Hunt is not the same as the Rite of Dedication from earlier editions: it's not necessary for <i>any</i> member of the pack to take it if they don't want to. If a group wants to play that way, there's nothing stopping them. And no pressure to get it (though the benefits of having it are great: I love how it's a Beat generator, and it's a good way to &quot;convince&quot; spirits to grant you new Gifts, but it's not the <i>only</i> way.<br /> <br /> Not having Sacred Hunt isn't a major disadvantage for your characters, all it does is present them with a unique set of dramatic obstacles to overcome. Which is exactly why everybody's playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:11:49-08:00","id":1047915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047860#post1047860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>If any local Tribes or Protectorate thinks straight, they will not agree with you on this - because Harmony is making you in check with Death Rage, giving tools to maintaining it it should be <i>first thing you teach to new </i>Uratha, with packs or not.</b> Stoping Harmony automatic Breaking Points Rite seems like this kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately tribes are not a formal authority and protectorates are rare. If they want to each everyone the sacred rite, that's their business, but they are not arbiters of Harmony and there's plenty of things that make werewolves death rage already. <br /> <br /> The point of the rite is to hunt. It's to call upon the ancient predator. Stopping Breaking Points is a side benefit, and something they have to do because, again, they do not belong here, this world is not theirs, and they have to bargain with extradimensional forces in order to pretend like they do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also,<b> being without pack maybe not your own choice</b> - Uratha leads violent lives, many times in books are described ones that lost their old packs and have 'lone survivor' syndrom over them. Not to mentions area when you are only pack in nearby, and suddenly your packmates are dead. So no, sometimes going without Sacred Hunt Rite is not your choice. </div> </div> </div>Now you're not making sense again. You said you understand the in-world reason why its needed and went back to arguing about the Experience cost and now you're bringing up in-world reasons again.<br /> <br /> If your pack is all dead and you don't have the rite you can learn it from a totem, you can learn it from a spirit, you can travel to another pack. Or you can suffer, which is the most likely end for a werewolf who's all alone. It happens. Because the life of the Uratha is not a regimented and easily controlled affair. Because sometimes people die, and sometimes people can't lead the hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, I did mark that I understand why Sacred Hunt should <b>not</b> be learn automatic - only that's it overpriced as 2 dot one. </div> </div> </div>You're overestimating the ability it takes to learn a 2 dot rite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, I beg to differ on society argument - being part of Tribes, packs and Lodges comes with other bonuses making staying with society worthwhile. Ha, I even go with other gameplay from other <b>CoD</b> game - Does making <i>High Speech</i> Merit free bonus for sticking with Orders in Mage make it more compelling to join them or not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>It's not that similar, but considering how necessary the language of magic is to mages and how useful the Mantra yantra is, yes, it is likely a selling point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Totally wrong - existing of Gauntlet, dichotomy of Flesh and Spirit, or even simple lack of Wolf with us now are reasons to rise Pangaea again - and by this, why it's loss was a shock. Just read <b>Pure</b> book - there are at least a dozen arguments why to make return of Pangaea thing, from Uratha perspective. It's just very bad idea for humanity. </div> </div> </div>And before we had the Neolithic section, before second edition made things more concrete, you could look at the Gauntlet, the Gurihal and Hisil, and say 'It had always been that way, werewolves are just some sort of Claimed-descendants, there is no Father Wolf, there was no Pangaea, and the Pure are chasing a lost cause.'<br /> <br /> It was a myth and before the evidence we've been given in second edition, there was no argument that could prove otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I <b><i>never</i></b> said there should be change on this part of mechanics. I'm all in for Breaking Points or Essence bleeds - just young pups should start much easier w Sacred Hunt Rite itself, if it is so 'sacred' to being Uratha. If Hunt is like prayer, each character should be able to do this, not only one that choose this common Rite for any other. Virtually <i>all</i> Uratha should be able to commerce Sacred Hunt. </div> </div> </div>They didn't build churches in everyone's house. You go to church to pray, because it's a communal thing. If you don't, you sit at home worshiping on your own, you're disassociating yourself from the community and risk further Breaking Points<br /> <br /> They are able to choose Sacred Hunt, but there's no reason to if someone else is a ritemaster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Invalid part of argument, as you clearly totally missed my point. Hunt is needed in game - it's just weird it's so costly for starting characters to do it themselves. </div> </div> </div>It's free. You're attributing an amount of time and study to it that isn't part of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Setting as written seems to be different here with you - all it's say that if <i>pack is all good</i>, you do not need Rite. Situation like those are... not often. Not to mention that each Tribe and Lodge have their own Rite's variant, so it's <b><i>beneficial </i></b>for the pack to have multiple Sacred Hunt ritemasters, not only on the reason of 'our Ithaeur is barely living and cannot make us Rite'. I literally have example of this in our game. </div> </div> </div>It <i>is</i> beneficial for a pack to have multiple people who know the Sacred Hunt, but it's not necessary. Just like it's beneficial for everyone to have great combat skills, great tracking skills, great social skills, great mental skills and great sorceries. But it's not necessary, and not realistic.<br /> <br /> Your situation is your own, I don't know why your Ithaeur is out of commission for several months, but one of the other members of the pack could have learned the rite, or they can all seek out another ritemaster to learn it.<br /> <br /> What you're describing is the kind of situation werewolves get in. What you're proposing is eliminating an entire aspect of the struggle of being a werewolf because one pack is having a hard time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:14:01-08:00","id":1047916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047877#post1047877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well forsaken 1st edition didnt had the hunt rite or at least not in the same way as it is now and Uratha &quot;society&quot; such as it is was fine and &quot;working&quot;. I have my issues on how contradictory it was but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>It did have the Sacred Hunt Rite, it was the only way to get Gifts and one of the few ways to kill spirits, as they were a lot tougher to destroy then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would say that i doubt werewolf who suffer from breaking points for not hunting do so for just not getting the 2XP worth of a rite. Most likely they are on the whole peter parker plot of &quot;i dont wanna be spiderman anymore and just be regular human.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Which is a valid option to play. One of the example ghost wolves is like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047893#post1047893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thats kind of proving Wyrdhamster point, one player at least have to bite the bullet to have this thing that is needed to play the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why they all get free rite dots. There's not enough rituals around to warrant an entire party of players clamoring over them. And being a flawed werewolf is a major part of the game. Having the sacred hunt is needed to be a good werewolf, it's not needed to play the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-12-2017, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:18:59-08:00","id":1047917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047888#post1047888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need to know Sacred Hunt to prevent Harmony Breaking Points, you just need to participate in Siskur-Dah. The Rite can be performed by someone else. And even if you don't have anyone who can do the Rite for you, you can always compensate by hitting Breaking Points in the opposite direction.<br /> <br /> Yes, that is a risk you take in choosing not to learn the Sacred Hunt Rite yourself. If you don't find that to be an acceptable risk, take Sacred Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I mentioned, when your Ithaeur is mascaraed, you are in deep trouble, unless you start to break in other way, breaking Oaths of Moon. It's totally uncool to have this 'needed costs' for PCs. It's really 'gameplay tax' like now it is. Sacred Hunt should be cheap or free if it's so central to characters.<br /> <br /> I'm surely will house rules when running game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047888#post1047888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is always the player's choice not to take the Sacred Hunt Rite with their free Rite dots. If that choice leads to consequences down the line, good. Consequences are what stories are built on.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Choice</i> is good for story. Punishing players for not spending points in central premise of the game - which should be free - is surely not good for <i>at least</i> one table - mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047888#post1047888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like a strange thing to get hung up on, considering the character creation rules give you enough free Rite dots to buy it. I'm sure if it had been a 1 dot Rite, you would only have gotten 1 free Rite dot at character creation, and 2 seems like a reasonable cost for the benefits it gives.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's commodity should lower the cost - like I pointed before - like <i>every</i> Tribes Uratha should learn it, sooner or later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047888#post1047888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a very good analogy, since you only get High Speech for free if you're in an Order, but you get two dots of Rites for free even if you're a Ghost Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is also buffling me - <b>if you are Ghost Wolf, game assumes you <i>did not</i> went with Tribes training. I can see some spirits teach you particular Rite or two - but Rites Trait?</b> It seems a bit artificial 'we made 2 Rite that everyone in game should use - okay, let's give everyone free Rites 2 Trait, even if it's not logical'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047888#post1047888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Nofather was getting at is that if there was no possibility of starting without Sacred Hunt, then the Breaking Points and Essence Bleed for not going on Siskur-Dah would be pretty pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I think that Rite 1 dot cost is optimal solution - it's enough to cost something character, but also not making 'Mark, you NEED to take Sacred Hunt, as everyone need ritemaster for it - okay, thanks for not letting build my character as I want too' thing. Also, Ghost Wolves should not start automatically with it, from in setting point of view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047888#post1047888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going on Siskur-Dah is prayer. Performing the Sacred Hunt Rite is <i>leading your pack in prayer</i>. Virtually all Uratha <i>do</i> participate in Siskur-Dah, but they don't all lead the Rite, just like not all Christians lead a congregation.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <i>every</i> Christian ( or at least Catholic ) knows Lord's Prayer ( called also Our Lord ) and can make it, if it's needed. Priest is chosen on mass only as 'best suited for the role', but in dire need or when priests are not available, ANY Christian can make those. In Catholic Church, for examples, anyone can make Anointing of the Sick - from priests it's just to comes with 'better effects'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047888#post1047888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two experiences is not &quot;so costly&quot;. It's the same price as a single dot in a Skill. And you get it for free at character creation if you want it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It IS cost of single dot in Skill. It is costly for most common Ritual in game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047888#post1047888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if that risk ends up biting you in the ass, that creates drama for the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it creates 'character tax' - and un-needed group frustration. In 2E, I choose Tribes for their Prey also - and that means that I want to be <i>good </i>at hunting those. If I choose Strom Lord because I want character to hunt Ridden, costly Sacred Hunt is 'character tax' in my eyes - and well, everyone I play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-12-2017, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:27:48-08:00","id":1047927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047916#post1047916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why they all get free rite dots. There's not enough rituals around to warrant an entire party of players clamoring over them. And being a flawed werewolf is a major part of the game. Having the sacred hunt is needed to be a good werewolf, it's not needed to play the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Practically? No, to play <b>Werewolf </b>2E you <i>need</i> Sacred Hunt - it's so central mechanics, without it you miss like half of your characters options. And not talking here about things like setting implications or just good old 'Our game is about Hunt as Ritual' - limiting Sacred Hunt is just artificially limit game itself. It's just bad game design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:28:50-08:00","id":1047928,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets\">You've had this argument before.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047927#post1047927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Practically? No, to play <b>Werewolf </b>2E you <i>need</i> Sacred Hunt - it's so central mechanics, without it you miss like half of your characters options. And not talking here about things like setting implications or just good old 'Our game is about Hunt as Ritual' - limiting Sacred Hunt is just artificially limit game itself. It's just bad game design.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't miss any options. All you miss is the sacred hunt. If you're playing a game that takes place over the in-world course of a weekend, you wouldn't even miss it and are still capable of doing everything werewolves do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:39:37-08:00","id":1047938,"title":"","content":"Half of Gifts are connected to having Siskur-Dah Condition - so you, literally, miss half of your characters options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:40:03-08:00","id":1047939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047893#post1047893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because its a lie of a choice, is giving then the choice but then there is only 1 option that is not gonna cripple them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in the same sense that putting 4 of your starting Arrtibute dots into Strength, 1 into Decterity, and leaving Stamina at 1 is &quot;a lie of a choice&quot;. Distributing character creation freebie points is <i>always</i> a tradeoff between specialization and generalization. If you want to build that redundancy into your pack so that you are never without someone who can do Sacred Hunt, you do so at the cost of having a greater variety of Rites available to your pack. If you choose to diversify your Rites, you do so at the risk of the person or people with Sacred Hunt being injured, captured, or killed. I call that a meaningful choice, because there are benefits and drawbacks to both options. If you, personally, don't think diversifying is ever worth the risk, that's your prerogative. In personally glad the option is available, because I, personally, think it is almost always worth the risk. Different strokes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:42:08-08:00","id":1047942,"title":"","content":"wyrd, at this point I believe you're going to the other extreme and having an exaggerated reaction to anything that even <i>looks </i>like a character tax to players. To the point that you're putting a good deal of your posts into arguing (not really <i>proving</i>) how costly it is, despite others saying that it's not that expensive, and how you're ignoring the benefits of having the story of how the werewolf came to lack the rite, and what potential drama could be drawn from lacking the rite. Not to mention refuting possible settings and story developments, just because it doesn't mesh with your dead-set views on the Siskur Dah.<br /> <br /> The game isn't taxing you on necessary arrangements, because you can play without it. More like an end-game content DLC that everyone downloads because it's cheap and satisfying. But you aren't convinced, are you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:49:20-08:00","id":1047947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047938#post1047938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Half of Gifts are connected to having Siskur-Dah Condition - so you, literally, miss half of your characters options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only six gifts rely on the Condition. Each 3-dot Moon Gift and Tireless Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T15:52:30-08:00","id":1047951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047938#post1047938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Half of Gifts are connected to having Siskur-Dah Condition - so you, literally, miss half of your characters options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if no one in the pack takes it. If at least one character takes it, everyone else gets access to all of those character options. If that character dies or is otherwise out of commission, you only lose access to those character options temporarily, until someone else in the pack takes it, or the player who's character died or whatever comes back with a new character that has it. In the mean time, your pack experiences some great story-worthy drama as their forced to struggle and sacrifice to counteract their gradual shift towards Flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T16:19:05-08:00","id":1047975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047917#post1047917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I mentioned, when your Ithaeur is mascaraed, you are in deep trouble, unless you start to break in other way, breaking Oaths of Moon. It's totally uncool to have this 'needed costs' for PCs. It's really 'gameplay tax' like now it is. Sacred Hunt should be cheap or free if it's so central to characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The situation you're describing that your players are in sounds like an awesome story to me. It's not a gameplay tax if not paying it creates <i>more</i> interesting gameplay scenarios.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047917#post1047917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surely will house rules when running game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, have fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047917#post1047917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Choice</i> is good for story. Punishing players for not spending points in central premise of the game - which should be free - is surely not good for <i>at least</i> one table - mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a punishment, it's a natural consequence of your choices. If your players didn't want to risk the possibility of their only ritemaster with Sacred Hunt being out of commission, they should have had one or two more of them take Sacred Hunt with their completely free character creation dots. They decided it was worth the risk. That choice has consequences. It's no more a gameplay tax than the Medicine skill - if your group only has one character with dots in Medicine and that character dies, you have to deal with nobody being able to do first aid. If that's not an acceptable risk to the players, more of them should invest in the Medicine skill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047917#post1047917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's commodity should lower the cost - like I pointed before - like <i>every</i> Tribes Uratha should learn it, sooner or later.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cost is literally nothing if you want to take it. Those dots are FREE. It only costs actual experiences if you made the conscious choice not to take it, and to take something else instead. And at that point, its cost is exactly the same as what you would have paid for the Rite or Rites you took instead. Its cost after character creation <i>should be</i> proportional to its benefits. Then it becomes a non-choice, because if it's cheaper to spend your starting dots on another Rite and take Sacred Hunt later (or vice versa), then that's what the self-interested player will always do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047917#post1047917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is also buffling me - <b>if you are Ghost Wolf, game assumes you <i>did not</i> went with Tribes training. I can see some spirits teach you particular Rite or two</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Convenient, because two is exactly the amount you get for free at character creation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047917#post1047917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It seems a bit artificial 'we made 2 Rite that everyone in game should use - okay, let's give everyone free Rites 2 Trait, even if it's not logical'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see anything illogical about it. Werewolves can learn Rites from spirits, so there's no reason a Ghost Wolf shouldnt be able to learn the two starting dots worth of Rites that an Uratha can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047917#post1047917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I think that Rite 1 dot cost is optimal solution - it's enough to cost something character, but also not making 'Mark, you NEED to take Sacred Hunt, as everyone need ritemaster for it - okay, thanks for not letting build my character as I want too' thing. Also, Ghost Wolves should not start automatically with it, from in setting point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd, giving dots of Rites instead of giving Sacred Hunt for free only gives you more options for building your character the way you want. If Sacred Hunt was a 1-dot Rite, you would probably only get 1 free dot of Rites at character creation. If it was a 3-dot Rite, you would get 3 dots of Rites at character creation. 2 is just the most reasonable cost for what the Rite does, and you always have the option of starting with it if you want to start with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047917#post1047917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, <i>every</i> Christian ( or at least Catholic ) knows Lord's Prayer ( called also Our Lord ) and can make it, if it's needed. Priest is chosen on mass only as 'best suited for the role', but in dire need or when priests are not available, ANY Christian can make those. In Catholic Church, for examples, anyone can make Anointing of the Sick - from priests it's just to comes with 'better effects'.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not every Christian can administer the Host, which is a more apt analogy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047917#post1047917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It IS cost of single dot in Skill. It is costly for most common Ritual in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>A single dot in a skill is <i>peanuts</i>! It's literally the second least anything in the game can cost!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047917#post1047917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it creates 'character tax' - and un-needed group frustration. In 2E, I choose Tribes for their Prey also - and that means that I want to be <i>good </i>at hunting those. If I choose Strom Lord because I want character to hunt Ridden, costly Sacred Hunt is 'character tax' in my eyes - and well, everyone I play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, if you want Sacred Hunt, you can have it from character creation at absolutely no cost. That's not a tax. The only difference between the way the rule works now, and if you gave Sacred Hunt to everyone for free, is that those of us who aren't so paranoid about being without access to the Rite wouldnt have the option of taking something else instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T17:57:25-08:00","id":1048004,"title":"","content":"Personally i dont think is such a game breaking thing. Either make hunt rite a 1 dot rite and you get 2 at chargen. Or leave it at 2 dots but give 3 dots of rite at chargen.<br /> <br /> That said the argument that the hunt rite is not necesary for a party is like saying that mysteries arent a necesary part of playing awakening. While i agree that it shouldny the game sure does like to hammer in that the hunt is the be-all-end-all of the forsaken game experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T18:21:23-08:00","id":1048011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048004#post1048004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally i dont think is such a game breaking thing. Either make hunt rite a 1 dot rite and you get 2 at chargen. Or leave it at 2 dots but give 3 dots of rite at chargen.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, of course it won't break your game if you want to run it that way, but it's not broken the way it's written either. The way it's written, you get Sacred Hunt for free unless you don't want to get Sacred Hunt, in which case you get an equivalent value in other Rites as compensation. What you and Wyrd are proposing is a way to get Sacred Hunt <i>and </i>other Rites without having to use your character creation Merit dots on them. That's what it comes down to, you want to have your cake and eat it too. And that's <i>fine</i> if you want to run your games that way, but don't make it about the system as-written not working.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048004#post1048004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said the argument that the hunt rite is not necesary for a party is like saying that mysteries arent a necesary part of playing awakening. While i agree that it shouldny the game sure does like to hammer in that the hunt is the be-all-end-all of the forsaken game experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is making the argument that Sacred Hunt isn't necessary for the party. It's just not necessary for <i>everyone in the party</i> to have. As long as one person has it (or one person from each Tribe if you want access to all the tribe-specific bonuses), you don't need anyone else to take it, unless you want that back-up in case something happens to the guy who has it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:28:45-08:00","id":1048081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047938#post1047938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Half of Gifts are connected to having Siskur-Dah Condition - so you, literally, miss half of your characters options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demonstrably wrong. As nofather says, 6 facets actually require Siskur-Dah, one gains a bonus on exceptional success if the prey of a Sikur-Dah is in the area, and that prey could be subject to any sacred hunt, it doesn't have to have anything to do with the Uratha using the Gift.<br /> <br /> So, 6.5 out of 115 facets being half is a bit of a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:37:52-08:00","id":1048084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048081#post1048081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demonstrably wrong. As nofather says, 6 facets actually require Siskur-Dah, one gains a bonus on exceptional success if the prey of a Sikur-Dah is in the area, and that prey could be subject to any sacred hunt, it doesn't have to have anything to do with the Uratha using the Gift.<br /> <br /> So, 6.5 out of 115 facets being half is a bit of a stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, every character with 3 or more dots in their primary Auspice will have 1 of those 6. But yeah, calling it &quot;half&quot; is excessive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:38:49-08:00","id":1048085,"title":"","content":"Beside the idea of 'I need to take Sacred Hunt for the team, thank you very much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />' , I plan to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1006024-open-table-model-with-cod-games\">run Open Table game</a> - Where from the constructions of game, you do not know with WHO you will play next time, at least half of characters should have Sacred Hunt to make it work.<br /> <br /> So still I opt for the lowering cost of Sacred Hunt to 1 dot with giving characters free 2 dots of Rite Trait. Less 'life choice on chargen', more 'most character should take those'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:44:29-08:00","id":1048090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048085#post1048085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beside the idea of 'I need to take Sacred Hunt for the team, thank you very much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />' , I plan to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1006024-open-table-model-with-cod-games\">run Open Table game</a> - Where from the constructions of game, you do not know with WHO you will play next time, at least half of characters should have Sacred Hunt to make it work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a situation where players would be well-advised to take Sacred Hunt with their free Rite dots. Much like players who go to D&amp;D Encounters would be well-advised to have some healing potions handy because you can't count on there being a healer from week to week.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048085#post1048085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So still I opt for the lowering cost of Sacred Hunt to 1 dot with giving characters free 2 dots of Rite Trait. Less 'life choice on chargen', more 'most character should take those'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most characters probably <i>should </i>take Sacred Hunt at character creation, even without the house rule, unless they know someone else in the pack already has it, and even then it's not a bad choice.<br /> <br /> You need to stop thinking of those 2 free dots as character customization options and start thinking of them as Sacred Hunt as a template ability, that you have the option to trade in for 2 dots of Rites if for some reason you don't want Sacred Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T23:47:39-08:00","id":1048092,"title":"","content":"Let's be clear here. Siskur-Dah is an important part of the 2nd ed Uratha experience, but <i>it's not essential</i>. That's why it's not automatic.<br /> <br /> Narratively, there are many, many stories that can be told without the sacred hunt. Using Wyrd's example, you could lose the only ritemaster who knew the rite and explore the difficulties that befall the pack. You could play a group of young Uratha taken under the wings of an experienced pack, so the elders call the sacred hunt and lead the younger pack. You could have the pack all invest in an ancient mentor who calls the Siskur-Dah and points the pack at his enemies. Eventually the pack realises how they've been used and struggle to break their bonds and redeem themselves.<br /> <br /> None of these games are possible if Siskur-Dah is automatic to every character. If it was, you'd have to house rule to take it away. There's your character tax.<br /> <br /> But let's look at mechanics. If you go beyond your Primal Urge Hunt Time and don't have access to Siskur-Dah, <i>all that happens is you lose a point of Essence per day and suffer a breaking point towards Flesh</i>. That's it. You don't go insane, or wither away and lose health levels until you die. One point of Essence, one breaking point towards Flesh. That's practically nothing. Go eat a human for the Essence and woah, you've counter-balanced the breaking point as well. (Yes, I know breaking points aren't auto shift, but you get the point.)<br /> <br /> The point is, no matter how much Wyrd oversells the absolute dire need for Siskur-Dah by every werewolf, the penalties for not having it are so small that it's in no way a requirement. It's designed to be an irritant, but it's not insurmountable by any stretch of the imagination.<br /> <br /> Is it preferable for a pack to have access to the rite? Sure. Does it make a werewolf's life more difficult by not having it? Sure. That's drama. Drama makes the game.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the default assumption is that a pack will take Siskur-Dah with their free rite dots. It's even assumed several members of the pack will take it so they can benefit from various different hunt bonuses.<br /> <br /> But stop pretending werewolves can't live without Siskur-Dah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T02:13:28-08:00","id":1048132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048092#post1048092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narratively, there are many, many stories that can be told without the sacred hunt. Using Wyrd's example, you could lose the only ritemaster who knew the rite and explore the difficulties that befall the pack. You could play a group of young Uratha taken under the wings of an experienced pack, so the elders call the sacred hunt and lead the younger pack. You could have the pack all invest in an ancient mentor who calls the Siskur-Dah and points the pack at his enemies. Eventually the pack realises how they've been used and struggle to break their bonds and redeem themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so we have dichotomy between narrative and mechanics here - from corebook read I assumed that full werewolf temple was meaning young Uratha <i>after </i>of Tribes introduction and trening, like you start in <b>Mage</b>. Now you written here that it has been written to be starting as semi dependent group on older Uratha. So why start with 2 Rite Trait dots in the first place, if character will not be independent?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048092#post1048092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But let's look at mechanics. If you go beyond your Primal Urge Hunt Time and don't have access to Siskur-Dah, <i>all that happens is you lose a point of Essence per day and suffer a breaking point towards Flesh</i>. That's it. You don't go insane, or wither away and lose health levels until you die. One point of Essence, one breaking point towards Flesh. That's practically nothing. Go eat a human for the Essence and woah, you've counter-balanced the breaking point as well. (Yes, I know breaking points aren't auto shift, but you get the point.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell this to all those young Ghost Wolves Uratha that in matter of days lose Harmony because they cannot invoke Sacred Hunt. From my read of rules, once you were hit with Essence Bleed and Harmony Breaking Point, you lose them <i>daily</i>. Maybe I'm weird, but Tribes would want to avoid this at any price, so they would not need hungry for flesh pups only because they lost pack or their ritemaster is out of action for weeks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048092#post1048092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it preferable for a pack to have access to the rite? Sure. Does it make a werewolf's life more difficult by not having it? Sure. That's drama. Drama makes the game.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the default assumption is that a pack will take Siskur-Dah with their free rite dots. It's even assumed several members of the pack will take it so they can benefit from various different hunt bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is differance between drama and making illogical conclusions on setting. You also made my point when marking that you made rules so at least one character in pack need to use all his Rites dots on Sacred Hunt, for each group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048092#post1048092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But stop pretending werewolves can't live without Siskur-Dah.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's you that written game and setting this way in first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T02:26:42-08:00","id":1048135,"title":"","content":"This is one of the strangest threads I've seen in a while.<br /> <br /> On Sacred Hunt as a rite rather than an innate power:<br /> \u200b - It's a rite because, metaphysically, in the setting, what the Sacred Hunt does <i>is a rite</i>.<br /> <br /> On giving the Sacred Hunt rite for free:<br /> - The game <i>does that</i>\u200b. You start with 2 free dots, which you can spend on Sacred Hunt <i>\u200bbut you don't have to</i>\u200b. I find it bizarre that if we'd simply said 'you get the Sacred Hunt rite', we'd have avoided this entire issue but provided players with less flexibility and freedom for their character choices.<br /> <br /> On making the Sacred Hunt a 1-dot rite:<br /> \u200b - It doesn't matter how many dots we made it, this argument would still be the same; the goalposts would just shift. Regardless, it's 2 dots because that's where what it does lies in the costing structure for rites.<br /> <br /> On taking rites other than the Sacred Hunt with the free dots:<br /> \u200b - There is absolutely no issue with doing so in play or in setting. Seriously. I've run several games under the 2e ruleset and regularly had a mix of characters starting with the Sacred Hunt and those not. It works absolutely fine every time.<br /> <br /> On the Sacred Hunt as a tax rite:<br /> \u200b - It's bloody well not. I spent a long time hewing out the admin rites from the game; Sacred Hunt not only <i>\u200bdoes something meaningful</i>\u200b but there are benefits to having multiple pack members with it; equally, not having it is not the end of the world. I'm not sure why there's such a focus on an ithaeur having it, given that an ithaeur is no better at it than anyone else. Regardless, if you're the one person in a pack who takes Sacred Hunt, you're not shouldering the 'rite tax' burden while your mates all get to pick cool rites. You're the one in the position of <i>power</i>\u200b. <i>You</i>\u200b get to choose what the pack actually subjects to the Sacred Hunt and what isn't worthy. <i>You</i>\u200b get to push the focus onto your favoured prey, as it'll just be your Tribal benefit that the pack has access to.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd for characters who choose something else, that's absolutely fine. In-character as well as out of character. It's trivial to think up justifications as to why a pack would happily have a mix of knowledge.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T02:45:42-08:00","id":1048140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048132#post1048132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tell this to all those young Ghost Wolves Uratha that in matter of days lose Harmony because they cannot invoke Sacred Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey, young Ghost Wolves Uratha, after about 3 months of not participating in a sacred hunt, you'll begin to break towards Flesh each day. This is easily mitigated in a number of ways, all of which Wyrd seems to ignore in continuing his fallacious argument.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048132#post1048132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my read of rules, once you were hit with Essence Bleed and Harmony Breaking Point, you lose them <i>daily</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad that's what you read, because it's exactly what it says and exactly what I wrote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048132#post1048132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm weird, but Tribes would want to avoid this at any price,</div> </div> </div> </div>Tribes aren't monolithic entities. How individual Uratha choose to deal with their existence is their own choice. Everyone have the rite, no-one have the rite, it's up to the pack. They can sort their own shit out. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048132#post1048132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is differance between drama and making illogical conclusions on setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes there is, but across numerous game lines, you don't seem to grasp that your opinion doesn't pass for logical conclusion. Do what you want in your game, that's fine. Argue your point, that's fine. But many other people here, including many writers who discussed and debated these issues for months/years before ink ever touched paper, don't agree with your belief that it is illogical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048132#post1048132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's you that written game and setting this way in first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. As demonstrated by ideas and mechanics, it's entirely not what we wrote in the first place. We wrote the wolf must hunt, not the wolf must sacred hunt.<br /> <br /> (And I've never pretended that life is easy for a werewolf who doesn't get regular sacred hunts. But they can survive.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T02:49:23-08:00","id":1048142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048135#post1048135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Sacred Hunt as a rite rather than an innate power:<br /> \u200b - It's a rite because, metaphysically, in the setting, what the Sacred Hunt does <i>is a rite</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand this from at least few posts in frist page, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048135#post1048135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On giving the Sacred Hunt rite for free:<br /> - The game <i>does that</i>\u200b. You start with 2 free dots, which you can spend on Sacred Hunt <i>\u200bbut you don't have to</i>\u200b. I find it bizarre that if we'd simply said 'you get the Sacred Hunt rite', we'd have avoided this entire issue but provided players with less flexibility and freedom for their character choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we have other definition 'for free' then - if my characters need to take Sacred Hunt to let all other players play in setting as intended (i.e. pack declaring Sacred Hunt when needed ) and other pack members can goes without it, I'm one Rite less. Rite that should any Uratha get. It's not free - maybe it's not tax, but it's clearly putting at least one character ins pack 'you must do this so we have our characters better'. It's not fair, and could be missed with other design principles. And clearly it's not 'free' if at least one character need to take it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048135#post1048135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On making the Sacred Hunt a 1-dot rite:<br /> \u200b - It doesn't matter how many dots we made it, this argument would still be the same; the goalposts would just shift. Regardless, it's 2 dots because that's where what it does lies in the costing structure for rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not understand this - clearly Tribes members would want as much Uratha to know this, as it's basis of their society. It's also not very much powerful than 1 dot Rites - but even if, Tribes society would simply make it cheaper just to make as much members as it can, to alivate probable problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048135#post1048135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Sacred Hunt as a tax rite:<br /> \u200b - It's bloody well not. I spent a long time hewing out the admin rites from the game; Sacred Hunt not only <i>\u200bdoes something meaningful</i>\u200b but there are benefits to having multiple pack members with it; equally, not having it is not the end of the world. I'm not sure why there's such a focus on an ithaeur having it, given that an ithaeur is no better at it than anyone else. Regardless, if you're the one person in a pack who takes Sacred Hunt, you're not shouldering the 'rite tax' burden while your mates all get to pick cool rites. You're the one in the position of <i>power</i>\u200b. <i>You</i>\u200b get to choose what the pack actually subjects to the Sacred Hunt and what isn't worthy. <i>You</i>\u200b get to push the focus onto your favoured prey, as it'll just be your Tribal benefit that the pack has access to.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd for characters who choose something else, that's absolutely fine. In-character as well as out of character. It's trivial to think up justifications as to why a pack would happily have a mix of knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not told that Sacred Hunt is not meaningful - but from setting as written in 2E it imply's that <i>every</i> Uratha should have Scared Hunt to commerce himself, at least from time to time. And even if not, it should be given as prevention from Essence Bleed and Harmony Breaking Points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-13-2017, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T03:16:25-08:00","id":1048151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048142#post1048142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we have other definition 'for free' then - if my characters need to take Sacred Hunt to let all other players play in setting as intended (i.e. pack declaring Sacred Hunt when needed ) and other pack members can goes without it, I'm one Rite less. Rite that should any Uratha get. It's not free - maybe it's not tax, but it's clearly putting at least one character ins pack 'you must do this so we have our characters better'. It's not fair, and could be missed with other design principles. And clearly it's not 'free' if at least one character need to take it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYour character doesn't need to take Sacred Hunt to let other players play in the setting as intended. That's a choice that you don't have to make, and claiming it is doesn't really help your case. It's also an argument you could trivially shift over to other rites, and indeed many other things beyond rites too.<br /> <br /> \u200bPlayers making statements to other players that 'you MUST get this so I don't have to', or players who have taken Sacred Hunt feeling resentful at players who have taken other rites, is something that a group should address because the problem clearly goes beyond the rite rules.<br /> <br /> \u200bFinally, the Sacred Hunt rite is a good thing to have for you as the individual player character; taking it doesn't mean you're 'taking one for the team' and sacrificing your own fun, it means you're getting access to an awesome and powerful rite attuned to your Tribal affinity. And if taking Sacred Hunt *is*, for you, sacrificing your own fun, then <i>don't take it</i>.<br /> <br /> Again, <i>we could have said everyone just gets Sacred Hunt</i> but instead we gave <i>more flexibility and choice</i>\u200b. I will not agree that this is somehow worse than just having mandated the 2 dots as having to be spent on Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not understand this - clearly Tribes members would want as much Uratha to know this, as it's basis of their society. It's also not very much powerful than 1 dot Rites - but even if, Tribes society would simply make it cheaper just to make as much members as it can, to alivate probable problems. </div> </div> </div>\u200bFirstly, no, Tribes don't demand everyone knows the Sacred Hunt. Most Uratha <i>want</i>\u200b it once they understand the world in which they now live. Tribes are not going to throw a tantrum just because there's a couple of werewolves in a pack who don't know it. For a pack that has no-one with it - great! You've got an excellent story hook right there! Pack outsiders looking in and trying to push forwards the Sacred Hunt element is a brilliant source of story and game under those circumstances, not a punishment.<br /> <br /> \u200bSecondly, the Tribes <i>can't make it cheaper,</i>\u200b any more than they can make buying Strength dots cheaper. Rite costs are not based on availability. It doesn't matter if everyone around you knows a rite to call down Hellions from the sun in a screaming bombardment of fire and destruction, it's still gonna be a 5-dot rite. If every Uratha in the world knew Sacred Hunt, it would still be a 2-dot rite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I did not told that Sacred Hunt is not meaningful - but from setting as written in 2E it imply's that <i>every</i> Uratha should have Scared Hunt to commerce himself, at least from time to time. And even if not, it should be given as prevention from Essence Bleed and Harmony Breaking Points. </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think you're incorrect on this, a number of other posters in this thread have already also expressed that they believe you're incorrect, and at this stage I'm not sure there's any reason to continue the discussion. Believe me, we very much considered things like 'tax' and admin choices. balance vs options, etc, when writing this stuff up. We've looked at it from that side of things, and I personally have played a lot of WtF2e since then that has made me comfortable in this particular decision. That's not true of everything in 2nd ed! There are some elements that, were I to go back in time, I'd ask to have done differently. 'Sacred Hunt/2 dots of rites' is not one of those, though. If this entire thread thus far hasn't convinced you to look at this from a different point of view from the one you started on, I suspect it's best if we just accept that an agreement is not going to be met.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn that case, play it how you like; give everyone the Sacred Hunt for free, or reduce to the cost to 1 dot, or whatnot. It's not going to break the game - we made it robust enough to manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T04:50:49-08:00","id":1048179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048135#post1048135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're the one in the position of <i>power</i>\u200b. <i>You</i>\u200b get to choose what the pack actually subjects to the Sacred Hunt and what isn't worthy. <i>You</i>\u200b get to push the focus onto your favoured prey, as it'll just be your Tribal benefit that the pack has access to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never seen this happened, mostly the player with the hunt serves the same function as a cleric in a party &quot;a hunt dispenser&quot; in this case. While fluff wise it might make sense gameplay wise either the threat of the week is not always the favored prey of the week. Or they just tell him not to be an ass as a player because that sounds like taking the ball home until the game centers around their PC.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;as it'll just be your Tribal benefit that the pack has access to.&quot; thats like saying not having an ithaeur in the party is making the rahu having his auspice benefits the one the pack has access to&quot; making the pack less useful in other situations doesnt really make your character shine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048092#post1048092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narratively, there are many, many stories that can be told without the sacred hunt. Using Wyrd's example, you could lose the only ritemaster who knew the rite and explore the difficulties that befall the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont see that much drama, i just see a new player having to bite the bullet and sacrifice 2XP. In the example is not the rite master and all his rite knowledge that the pack fells its lacking. Its the 2XP rite that as many have pointed out at least 1 person require to bite the bullet to get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048151#post1048151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Players making statements to other players that 'you MUST get this so I don't have to', or players who have taken Sacred Hunt feeling resentful at players who have taken other rites, is something that a group should address because the problem clearly goes beyond the rite rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been my experience in all the forsaken games i ran whether on the chargen rules or as cubs. On normal chargen it was &quot;okay who bites the bullet and gets the rite&quot; or they all take it wondering why bother to have the choice at all.<br /> <br /> As for cubs game, they complained that their first 2 dot of XP have to invariable go to this rite because it IS the necessary to play.<br /> <br /> However we usually play regular werewolf and not special case scenarios like this one<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048092#post1048092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You could play a group of young Uratha taken under the wings of an experienced pack, so the elders call the sacred hunt and lead the younger pack. You could have the pack all invest in an ancient mentor who calls the Siskur-Dah and points the pack at his enemies. Eventually the pack realises how they've been used and struggle to break their bonds and redeem themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>But this is my tables issues, is not a deal breaker by any means and is a easy corrected flaw of the game. So i agree with Wyrdhamster that it is a minor flaw of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 02-13-2017, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T05:02:38-08:00","id":1048185,"title":"","content":"Losing a dot of essence a day and needing to eat people occasionally is totally viable as a play style. It's how Vampire works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T05:14:44-08:00","id":1048193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048185#post1048185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Losing a dot of essence a day and needing to eat people occasionally is totally viable as a play style. It's how Vampire works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe - but cornering character in <i>needing</i> to do this, because he did not spend starting 2XP is... well, not fair in my POV.<br /> <br /> I will probably house rule issue on 1 dot Rite, as metaphysically I understand need for it to be Rite in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T06:14:57-08:00","id":1048207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048193#post1048193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe - but cornering character in <i>needing</i> to do this, because he did not spend starting 2XP is... well, not fair in my POV.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Three months</i>, wyrd. <i>Ninety days</i> of activity without gaining the benefits of a rite that is common enough to justify basically any werewolf NPC knowing it before you start suffering the issues werewolves suffer <i>that start to make them look like movie werewolves</i>. This does not translate into a risk of starvation until well, <i>well</i> into a werewolf's lifecycle \u2014 the way Harmony and Primal Urge are set up means that werewolves who aren't initiated into the culture of the Uratha sometimes wind up looking like serial killers.<br /> <br /> If you cannot justify characters who almost certainly learned the ropes of being a werewolf from other werewolves or creatures who know about them having some degree of access to an NPC that can perform the rite for them, <i>that is an issue with how you have constructed your setting, not a problem with the template.</i><br /> <br /> Also <i>your starting dots are not Experiences</i>. Nobody and nothing has said that you can liquidate your Attribute and Skill and Merit dots and Specialties into over a hundred Experiences and it's no more of a &quot;tax&quot; than the general expectation that you'll raise most of your Attributes to at least 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-13-2017, 09:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T06:43:09-08:00","id":1048213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048179#post1048179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have never seen this happened, mostly the player with the hunt serves the same function as a cleric in a party &quot;a hunt dispenser&quot; in this case. While fluff wise it might make sense gameplay wise either the threat of the week is not always the favored prey of the week. Or they just tell him not to be an ass as a player because that sounds like taking the ball home until the game centers around their PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is not an issue stemming from the game, though. I don't think it's really an issue at all, but inasmuch as you see it as a problem, it is resulting from you seeing the solution I laid out (which is just one of many possibilities) and not taking it. That's fine - it's your choice - but it's not like there aren't options available to resolve the issue you're having.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, do none of your players have characters with agendas, specific desires, opinions where they clash with other Uratha in the pack? Things like being the purse-keeper for the <i>\u200bsacred</i>\u200b rite of the hunt is... well, that's serious leverage if one chooses to use it. I can't do a lot about players who choose not to, though. We can't actually reach out into peoples' games, at the table, and demand they act differently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the &quot;as it'll just be your Tribal benefit that the pack has access to.&quot; thats like saying not having an ithaeur in the party is making the rahu having his auspice benefits the one the pack has access to&quot; making the pack less useful in other situations doesnt really make your character shine. </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's a very easy way for you to a) get spotlight time for your character and b) for your character to influence the pack into following their agenda. Again, if you choose not to do that, that's absolutely fine and you're not playing it wrong or anything, but it makes your assertion of this being a flaw as dubious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dont see that much drama, i just see a new player having to bite the bullet and sacrifice 2XP. In the example is not the rite master and all his rite knowledge that the pack fells its lacking. Its the 2XP rite that as many have pointed out at least 1 person require to bite the bullet to get. </div> </div> </div>\u200bI am saddened by the fact that you and Wyrd seem to see the Sacred Hunt as so dull a thing that being able to perform the rite is 'biting the bullet' rather than 'being able to perform a potent rite'. I will have to re-examine my own writing around the rite to see if the evocativeness and appeal of the description can be improved. However, I am entirely happy with the mechanical power of the rite, especially at its dot rating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This has been my experience in all the forsaken games i ran whether on the chargen rules or as cubs. On normal chargen it was &quot;okay who bites the bullet and gets the rite&quot; or they all take it wondering why bother to have the choice at all. </div> </div> </div><i>If you don't want to bother with the choice, you don't have to</i>. Again, we <i>literally added choice</i>\u200b; we gave more freedom because it suited both the IC elements pertaining to rites and the OC elements of player choice and game design. Plenty of player characters take advantage of the choice without causing their pack to founder or the Sacred Hunt ritemasters to feel resentful.<br /> <br /> \u200bLook, you clearly think the Sacred Hunt is well worth having in the first place, so why on earth would you treat it as 'biting the bullet' to pick it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for cubs game, they complained that their first 2 dot of XP have to invariable go to this rite because it IS the necessary to play. </div> </div> </div>\u200bBut... 2 dots of rites is something we gave for free. How you choose to implement increasing powers in a cubs game is not down to us. We literally have no control over how you and your players run that. If you choose to price free features as costing XP, that's really not on us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But this is my tables issues, is not a deal breaker by any means and is a easy corrected flaw of the game. So i agree with Wyrdhamster that it is a minor flaw of the game. </div> </div> </div>\u200bYou're correct that it's easily corrected. I assert that it is <i>not a flaw</i>. There are plenty of things in games that I disagree with or dislike, but I accept that they aren't necessarily flaws just because they don't jibe with my preferences.<br /> <br /> \u200bAgain, I point out that this whole debate descends from the fact that we said '2 free dots of rites' not 'Sacred Hunt'. It stems from us actually offering PCs and STs more choice to suit story situations, context, pack needs and the like. I am not going to apologise for us giving leeway rather than a straightjacket, and I find it bemusing that we have players who would not complain if they were <i>forced</i>\u200b to take the Sacred Hunt rite by the character creation rules, yet because there <i>is</i>\u200b some freedom in rite selection, complain about having to take the Sacred Hunt!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","user":"Acrozatarim","date":". 02-13-2017, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T06:50:37-08:00","id":1048216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048193#post1048193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe - but cornering character in <i>needing</i> to do this, because he did not spend starting 2XP is... well, not fair in my POV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, that character doesn't need to spend his 2 rites on it. If anyone in the pack has it, he doesn't have to deal with it. It's ridiculous that your acting as though every single werewolf needs to have it or they'll end up with breaking points every five minutes @_@","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:06:54-08:00","id":1048265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048207#post1048207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Three months</i>, wyrd. <i>Ninety days</i> of activity without gaining the benefits of a rite that is common enough to justify basically any werewolf NPC knowing it before you start suffering the issues werewolves suffer <i>that start to make them look like movie werewolves</i>. This does not translate into a risk of starvation until well, <i>well</i> into a werewolf's lifecycle \u2014 the way Harmony and Primal Urge are set up means that werewolves who aren't initiated into the culture of the Uratha sometimes wind up looking like serial killers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the other problem with RAW - this three months seems like... well, that you end up with serial killing Ghost Wolves only where there is absolutely <i>no one</i> Uratha in nearby that would not be in cubs territory any time in quarter of year. That is, virtually, unheard off. Maybe in Siberia or Alaska or some desert this can happen - but whenever you have in modern European country or America, a least 3 nearby packs would get your scent <i>before</i> this 90 days time limit. Once again, mechanics that not work with setting as written. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I would change starting Primal Urge to give one month before whole Essence Bleed and Harmony Breaking Points - you have one lunar month to find and stop First Changer. And yes, teach him Sacred Hunt - it's really first thing each Tribes member should do to newly found cub. I really <i>do not </i>see any reason why characters in setting would not teach this Rite them. Unless they want to risk breaking the Oaths of the Moon because of rampant cub from their stupid 'I need to control your Hunts'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048207#post1048207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you cannot justify characters who almost certainly learned the ropes of being a werewolf from other werewolves or creatures who know about them having some degree of access to an NPC that can perform the rite for them, <i>that is an issue with how you have constructed your setting, not a problem with the template.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Making sure each cub can declare Scared Hunt when his time limit goes is in best interest of whole Uratha population. i really do not see why you would <i>not</i> teach them Rite the first instance they can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:18:50-08:00","id":1048270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048213#post1048213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI am saddened by the fact that you and Wyrd seem to see the Sacred Hunt as so dull a thing that being able to perform the rite is 'biting the bullet' rather than 'being able to perform a potent rite'. I will have to re-examine my own writing around the rite to see if the evocativeness and appeal of the description can be improved. However, I am entirely happy with the mechanical power of the rite, especially at its dot rating.<br /> (...)<br /> \u200bAgain, I point out that this whole debate descends from the fact that we said '2 free dots of rites' not 'Sacred Hunt'. It stems from us actually offering PCs and STs more choice to suit story situations, context, pack needs and the like. I am not going to apologise for us giving leeway rather than a straightjacket, and I find it bemusing that we have players who would not complain if they were <i>forced</i>\u200b to take the Sacred Hunt rite by the character creation rules, yet because there <i>is</i>\u200b some freedom in rite selection, complain about having to take the Sacred Hunt!</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm not saying that Sacred Hunt is dull. I say it's freaking awesome! It's heart and soul of 2E game. I just really surprised it was not free for characters and I need to make some weird sheaningans at game table, becuase some players need to forsake ( :P ) part of their character concept to let groups fullfil <i>games premise </i>using this awesome power. Problem is with <i>forcing</i> it on players, where they should take it, one way or another. It's uncool and can lead to needless players drama.<br /> <br /> I question - If you needed to have Sacred Hunt and Rite pool in development - <b>Why not giving it for <i>free</i> for Tribes members?</b> It's cool and needed Rite, central to narrative of 2E. <b>Or w</b><b>hy not giving Sacred Hunt AND dot or two free to Rites, to let PCs customize thier characters?</b> Ghost Wolves could really start without it and we simple have the situation that is now at game tables - each Tribes pack members sooner or later ends with their own Sacred Hunt. Why making this needless choice at char gen that can end with bad relations in players party?<br /> <br /> It's like with High Speech Merit in Mage - in the and, every PC character ends with one. Even many of fan created Nameless Orders give High Speech in their write ups. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-13-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:22:25-08:00","id":1048272,"title":"","content":"You do know you can trade merit dots for more rites, right? That's a thing you can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:23:22-08:00","id":1048273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048265#post1048265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the other problem with RAW - this three months seems like... well, that you end up with serial killing Ghost Wolves only where there is absolutely <i>no one</i> Uratha in nearby that would not be in cubs territory any time in quarter of year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves don't <i>need</i> Essence until they're well past the threshold of superhuman potential and Primal Urge 1 means most conscientious Ghost Wolves without the rite are not going to <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe in Siberia or Alaska or some desert this can happen - but whenever you have in modern European country or America, a least 3 nearby packs would get your scent <i>before</i> this 90 days time limit. </div> </div> </div>Werewolves can't scent each other from further out than personal space, high Harmony specifically makes it more difficult to change forms, and the default form of a werewolf is the one that doesn't look any different from anybody else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Making sure each cub can declare Scared Hunt when his time limit goes is in best interest of whole Uratha population. i really do not see why you would <i>not</i> teach them Rite the first instance they can. </div> </div> </div>Wyrd, I realize you're an engineer, but biologically and economically redundancies are a waste of energy. Time spent teaching every werewolf how to invoke the Sacred Hunt when you only need one per pack is time spent not teaching them different useful tricks of the Shadow, and that's the difference between having Chain Rage or Hunting Ground or Wellspring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:28:33-08:00","id":1048279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048272#post1048272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know you can trade merit dots for more rites, right? That's a thing you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still basiclly boils down to 'Someone need to take Sacred Hunt on game start - this time it's you'. Rite should be: a) Free or b) Cheap ( like Rite is 1dot and you got 2 dots of Rite Trait ) - Other than this, someone <i>will </i>be doing sacrifices on character concept for the team. Some people will not have problem with that - others, not so much,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:54:10-08:00","id":1048293,"title":"","content":"You're playing a werewolf. It's within your concept.<br /> <br /> I mean, you can't buy everything at character creation. You have to pick which bits are the most relevant to you and work from there. This is no more a compromise than <i>literally every other decision you have to make when building a character.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 02-13-2017, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T10:07:47-08:00","id":1048297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048270#post1048270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm not saying that Sacred Hunt is dull. I say it's freaking awesome! It's heart and soul of 2E game. I just really surprised it was not free for characters and I need to make some weird sheaningans at game table, becuase some players need to forsake ( :P ) part of their character concept to let groups fullfil <i>games premise </i>using this awesome power. Problem is with <i>forcing</i> it on players, where they should take it, one way or another. It's uncool and can lead to needless players drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is forced to take it. You can play the game without it. If no one in the pack has it, you can still play the game. Granted, it will be a story about a pack of wolves struggling against the pull of disharmony, but that's there as an option because some people might want to play that way. If you don't want to play that way, you can take Sacred Hunt for free.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048270#post1048270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I question - If you needed to have Sacred Hunt and Rite pool in development - <b>Why not giving it for <i>free</i> for Tribes members?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>They do. That's what those <b>free</b> 2 dots of Rites are <i>for</i>.<br /> They could have just given Sacred Hunt for free and not given us the option to spend those dots on something else, but that would have been giving us fewer options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048270#post1048270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's cool and needed Rite, central to narrative of 2E. <b>Or why not giving Sacred Hunt AND dot or two free to Rites, to let PCs customize thier characters?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Because those dots aren't <i>for</i> customizing your character. They're for making sure anyone who wants Sacred Hunt can have it. If you don't want Sacred Hunt for some reason, doing it this way allows you to take something else of equal value instead, so that you're not starting out 2XP behind everyone who did start with Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048270#post1048270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Wolves could really start without it and we simple have the situation that is now at game tables - each Tribes pack members sooner or later ends with their own Sacred Hunt. Why making this needless choice at char gen that can end with bad relations in players party?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost Wolves <i>can</i> start without Sacred Hunt if that's the narrative they want to explore. And this way they don't have to start out 2XP behind everyone else if they make that choice. If having the option to take Sacred Hunt for free if you want it, or take something of equal value for free if you don't want it is creating bad relations between your players, that's not the rules' fault. You need to have a talk with your players because there's something else going on there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048270#post1048270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like with High Speech Merit in Mage - in the and, every PC character ends with one. Even many of fan created Nameless Orders give High Speech in their write ups. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but joining an Order just gives High Speech for free. The two free Rite dots in Werewolf are like if joining an Order gave you one free Merit dot. Everyone who wanted High Speech could still take it with that free Merit dot, and everyone who didn't want High Speech for some reason could spend that free Merit dot on something else so they wouldn't fall behind the players who did choose to take High Speech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T10:15:01-08:00","id":1048300,"title":"","content":"So... I have to just wonder what you'd be taking in place of Sacred Hunt? What's so critical at two dots here? Bottle spirit is pretty kick ass, admittedly, but that's Bone Shadow only. Chain Rage, Totemic Empowerment and Banish are pretty cool, but those are basically where you only need one person in the pack to take, and they're one dot each.<br /> <br /> If we have four PC wolves, that's 8 dots of rites. I'm actually hard pressed to really fill up all those dots if we spread them around. What's so critical here? Moon's Mad Love? Hunting Ground? I've never felt that impressed by them before. Handy, I suppose, but they're other &quot;bite the bullet for the pack&quot; type of rituals. Harness the Cycle, a ritual that can be used four times in an entire year?<br /> <br /> And that's not counting Wolfblooded ritualist NPCs that you can add to the pack at any time and can cast a few of the Pack Rites for the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-13-2017, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T10:24:40-08:00","id":1048307,"title":"","content":"You could burn two merit dots and get Fetish Creation. That's pretty useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T10:31:05-08:00","id":1048308,"title":"","content":"When making my character I was at a loss with what to do with Merit dots, there weren't that many options. The 'specialist' Auspice ones I didn't have enough Renown for and the Tribal one seemed redundant compared to some of the Auspice powers. So I ended up getting Embodiment of the Firstborn. My character wasn't big on rites so he just got Sacred Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T10:38:42-08:00","id":1048311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048279#post1048279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still basiclly boils down to 'Someone need to take Sacred Hunt on game start - this time it's you'.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could say the same thing about &quot;someone needs to have dots in Survival so we can actually track prey - this time it's you.&quot; First of all, you really don't <i>need</i> anyone to be able to track to play werewolf, but you are choosing to play a particular kind of story if you're choosing to play the pack without any trackers. Second of all, no one feels like &quot;great, I have to waste some of my starting Skill dots on Survival so the group has a tracker&quot; because tracking is <i>awesome</i> and something most werewolf players are going to want to be able to do, unless not being able to track is a specific part of their concept.<br /> <br /> The same is true of Sacred Hunt. You can play without it, but you are choosing a particular kind of story if you're choosing to be the pack who can't do Sacred Hunt, and nobody should be bothered by spending their free Rite dots on Sacred Hunt because it's an awesome Rite that most werewolf players are going to want to know, unless not knowing it is a specific part of their concept,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048270#post1048270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rite should be: a) Free or b) Cheap ( like Rite is 1dot and you got 2 dots of Rite Trait ) - Other than this, someone <i>will </i>be doing sacrifices on character concept for the team. Some people will not have problem with that - others, not so much,</div> </div> </div> </div>It is free if you want it. And if it was a 1-dot Rite, you would only get 1 free Rite dot at character creation because the purpose of that free dot is to make sure everyone who wants Sacred Hunt can have it for free, and to make sure everyone who doesn't want Sacred Hunt doesn't feel ripped off for choosing not to take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T11:12:25-08:00","id":1048327,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets\">Just dropping this in here in the hopes of it being useful for all parties.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T11:33:12-08:00","id":1048340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048308#post1048308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When making my character I was at a loss with what to do with Merit dots, there weren't that many options. The 'specialist' Auspice ones I didn't have enough Renown for and the Tribal one seemed redundant compared to some of the Auspice powers. So I ended up getting Embodiment of the Firstborn. My character wasn't big on rites so he just got Sacred Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously? I never have enough merit dots. Between the basic resources, allies/contacts, proffesional training and 1 style they run out pretty fast. And thats without taking into account werewolf specific merits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048213#post1048213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI mean, do none of your players have characters with agendas, specific desires, opinions where they clash with other Uratha in the pack? Things like being the purse-keeper for the <i>\u200bsacred</i>\u200b rite of the hunt is... well, that's serious leverage if one chooses to use it. I can't do a lot about players who choose not to, though. We can't actually reach out into peoples' games, at the table, and demand they act differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they do have but your scenario is a pretty specific one. Do character clash on their agendas? Sure. But for the sacred hunt to be used as leverage you have to have the rite master oppose the wishes of the rest of the party in NOT doing something they want to do. Does it cause drama? Not really, most likely they call the pc an ass and either hunt without it or bite the bullet and get the rite or just ask for a npc to do it for them. Afterwards the rest of the pack will get the rite and beat the PC senseless or kick him out for pulling that kind of thing. From a tabletop perspective the way to use the rite as leverage is for a player telling the other player they wont follow on the issue they wanna follow because he wont do his function. Its literally stopping the fun the rest of the party wants in.<br /> <br /> Its like a cleric refusing to heal the rest of the party when healing only takes 1 level. Yeah you call pull that exactly once before they kill your pc and force you to make another one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048213#post1048213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIt's a very easy way for you to a) get spotlight time for your character and b) for your character to influence the pack into following their agenda. Again, if you choose not to do that, that's absolutely fine and you're not playing it wrong or anything, but it makes your assertion of this being a flaw as dubious.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point was that being the only one in the party with the rite doesnt make your character shine because they only have access to your tribe bonus. It just draws attention on how they lack the tribe bonus for all the rest of the situations (unless the DM is doesnt put any of the other preys in the game)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048213#post1048213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI am saddened by the fact that you and Wyrd seem to see the Sacred Hunt as so dull a thing that being able to perform the rite is 'biting the bullet' rather than 'being able to perform a potent rite'. I will have to re-examine my own writing around the rite to see if the evocativeness and appeal of the description can be improved. However, I am entirely happy with the mechanical power of the rite, especially at its dot rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is from my and my player readings is that the game mention soooo much the hunt that kinda makes its such an integral part of the &quot;Forsaken experience&quot; that not taking it feels like a character creation trap. A game with a multitribe pack (all of them in my experience, but i have heards thats not always the case) assumes you got a sacred rite for all of them. And the rite itself, is doesnt feel like exaclty like a potent rite. It feels like a power everyone should have but not because its awesome but because is does many basic stuff needed to be a werewolf.<br /> <br /> If we were talking about any other rite, sure i dont see that much issue. But the sacred hunt rite feels like you are paying 2XP to play the game. And all the other options without it suggested dont feel organic, they feel like going out of you way to not use it as to prove a point. Like finding the perfect trail to go from one city to another in unicycle just to prove that cars arent necessary to travel from one city to another.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048185#post1048185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Losing a dot of essence a day and needing to eat people occasionally is totally viable as a play style. It's how Vampire works.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would say is more similarly to being a serial diablerist. Yes, its a viable playstyle as long as either the whole group is into it or the player accepts the idea that when its becomes known he is gonna be dead. Quoting a documental on discovery channel &quot;Nobody likes a cannibal&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T11:41:13-08:00","id":1048348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048340#post1048340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously? I never have enough merit dots. Between the basic resources, allies/contacts, proffesional training and 1 style they run out pretty fast. And thats without taking into account werewolf specific merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which goes to show, characters are made different. Mine didn't justify any Professional Training, still being young, and basically an on-the-run criminal he had no contacts or allies in the new place. He started with Alternate Identity 2, Eidetic Memory, Totem, and Embodiment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048340#post1048340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would say is more similarly to being a serial diablerist. Yes, its a viable playstyle as long as either the whole group is into it or the player accepts the idea that when its becomes known he is gonna be dead. Quoting a documental on discovery channel &quot;Nobody likes a cannibal&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not nearly that bad. A diablerist is literally addicted to eating other vampires. They have to roll to resist any 'reasonable' attempt to drain another vampire dry. A werewolf who eats humans has no such problem.<br /> <br /> They're not even really a cannibal, anyways. Uratha aren't human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-13-2017, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T11:45:36-08:00","id":1048353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048327#post1048327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets&amp;quot;]Just</a> dropping this in here in the hopes of it being useful for all parties.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>nofather beat you to it in post #29 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T11:49:47-08:00","id":1048355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048340#post1048340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its like a cleric refusing to heal the rest of the party when healing only takes 1 level. Yeah you call pull that exactly once before they kill your pc and force you to make another one.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't sound like a party that would get a new cleric very quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T11:51:48-08:00","id":1048356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048340#post1048340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its like a cleric refusing to heal the rest of the party when healing only takes 1 level. Yeah you call pull that exactly once before they kill your pc and force you to make another one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah.... honestly, I don't understand the point of this reference. First of all, clerics != healbots. Some clerics might be, but not all. There's plenty that aren't healers. They have other things to do with their spells when you could just chug a potion.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I've actually played a cleric in a game where I refused to heal some party members because they were outright insulting the gods my character worshiped. There's context involved in any decision. And no one killed my PC. Unsurprisingly, this is because the group isn't a bunch of murder-hobos. There's a lot going on, and games do have a lot of inter-character relationships beyond just &quot;combat roles.&quot; I used my character's healing ability as leverage to make a point. And I succeeded.<br /> <br /> Lastly? If you have a group that, for making an in-character choice, would kill your PC and force a new character on you? I think that group dynamic has some issues that need to be worked out in the first place. I certainly wouldn't play with such a group. If that's how you like playing, more power to you, but I would think that kind of game is the minority rather than the majority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T12:01:12-08:00","id":1048365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048340#post1048340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously? I never have enough merit dots. Between the basic resources, allies/contacts, professional training and 1 style they run out pretty fast. And thats without taking into account werewolf specific merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>But even at character creation you don't need to spend Merit points to get that ritual, since you get two dots of rituals free. So given that. I don't understand this point. Also I think the following has a good point:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=434486#post434486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I read it all, anyone could take the Siskur-Dah rite at character creation, but nobody in particular has to. What the rite does is start the hunt. What all of the werewolves need to do is go on such a hunt. One packmate can start it, everyone can go along. Everyone gets the condition, everyone fulfills there basic wolfy need.<br /> While anyone who knows the rite can call it on just about anything (be it a spirit to feed on for essence, a zoning proposal that needs to not pass legislation, or the Fire-Touched that killed your character's mom), the Tribal affiliation of the person leading the rite colors it to add strength against that Tribe's preferred prey. After all, it's what they've hunted more than anything else since time immemorial, so their hunts focus on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-13-2017, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T12:04:01-08:00","id":1048366,"title":"","content":"Plus there's difference between 'hunting' and the Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> Hunting is a natural inclination for every werewolf, it's part of their very being. And it's natural for a werewolf to, upon realizing what they've become, start hunting one way or another.<br /> <br /> But they don't belong here. And that hunt doesn't fulfill their spiritual needs for some reason. And they can get angry or try and resist but they'll still feel that pull and maybe they'll become mad butchers or think it's some horrible insanity and lock themselves up.<br /> <br /> The Sacred Hunt ameliorates that, bridging the gap between 'the hunt' and 'the Hunt' and allowing the Uratha to fit in, however temporarily.<br /> <br /> But it's not something every werewolf need know, because as social people, they tend to share one another's abilities. Wyrdhamster is in a position where, for whatever reason, the ritemaster is out of commission. Depending on their Primal Urge the other members of the pack have an option, where they can just bear through it until the ritemaster is healed, they can seek out any other pack, they can seek out a spirit or deal with their totem, or even just look for ancient werewolf lore and find where the rite has been recorded somewhere. This is a story entirely within the realms of Forsaken's setting. If he wants to have the Firstborn come down and grant every member of the party with free rites, that's fine too, but there's no reason the game should change because one group of player characters are encountering a setback.<br /> <br /> It's not a tax, it's not absolutely necessary, though it is obviously recommended for at least one person in a pack to have. It's not a requirement of half the gifts, it's not something every werewolf would know or would even want to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T12:10:33-08:00","id":1048372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048353#post1048353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> nofather beat you to it in post #29 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've noticed since.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T12:13:12-08:00","id":1048375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048365#post1048365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But even at character creation you don't need to spend Merit points to get that ritual, since you get two dots of rituals free. So given that. I don't understand this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing to the rite itself just seems strange to me give the quantity of merits in the 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048356#post1048356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly? If you have a group that, for making an in-character choice, would kill your PC and force a new character on you? I think that group dynamic has some issues that need to be worked out in the first place. I certainly wouldn't play with such a group. If that's how you like playing, more power to you, but I would think that kind of game is the minority rather than the majority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats isnt a in character choice as much as saying to the rest of the party &quot;do what i want or else you dont get the super necessary rite&quot;, to which the answer is a) the character gets beaten senseless b) they get a temporal solution or c) Another players gets the rite and they ignore the party member who tried to extort them or just kick him out of the pack. A in character choice would be more akin to &quot;cast the rite but dont participate on the hunt&quot;. Even from an in setting perspective the game sells you how the pack is above all else, so a member of the pack tries to extort the rest of the pack with something that while incredible necessary is ultimately 2 xp point easy to replace thing is in for a world of hurt or getting a new pack.<br /> <br /> What werewolf would want to have a packmember who is a petty wannabe tyrant who tries to extort the rest of the pack? Specially when he is 2xp points away to be replaceable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T12:34:50-08:00","id":1048382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048375#post1048375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What werewolf would want to have a packmember who is a petty wannabe tyrant who tries to extort the rest of the pack? Specially when he is 2xp points away to be replaceable</div> </div> </div> </div>But to fix that, only one other packmate has to learn it.<br /> <br /> And it's the same problem with every other ability. High Resources, Combat skills, Tracking, knowledge of the spirit. An Ithaeur can tell a spirits ban and bane at character creation. It's the first ability they learn at the first dot of Auspice renown. The difference between knowing and not knowing a spirits bane and ban are huge. Not knowing these things is a setback that can be dealt with through time and an investment someone makes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-13-2017, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T13:27:50-08:00","id":1048406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048340#post1048340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is from my and my player readings is that the game mention soooo much the hunt that kinda makes its such an integral part of the &quot;Forsaken experience&quot; that not taking it feels like a character creation trap.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you feel that way, then just take the Rite at character creation with your totally 100% free Rite dots. For those of us who feel that not taking Sacred Hunt is a viable option, let us take that option if we want to. Just because it looks like a trap to you doesn't mean the option shouldn't be available to others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048340#post1048340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A game with a multitribe pack (all of them in my experience, but i have heards thats not always the case) assumes you got a sacred rite for all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. The Tribe-specific bonuses are nice to have, but even less essential to play than Sacred Hunt itself. Many packs will <i>want</i> to have at least one member from each Tribe who knows it, but if they don't, that should be allowed too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048340#post1048340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the rite itself, is doesnt feel like exaclty like a potent rite. It feels like a power everyone should have but not because its awesome but because is does many basic stuff needed to be a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of what it does is needed to be a werewolf. Most of what it does makes a werewolf's life much easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048340#post1048340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we were talking about any other rite, sure i dont see that much issue. But the sacred hunt rite feels like you are paying 2XP to play the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You aren't paying 2XP for it, though. Those two character creation dots are <i>free</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048340#post1048340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And all the other options without it suggested dont feel organic, they feel like going out of you way to not use it as to prove a point. Like finding the perfect trail to go from one city to another in unicycle just to prove that cars arent necessary to travel from one city to another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who cares? Some people like riding unicycles and don't like driving cars. Don't outlaw unicycles just because you can't understand why someone would want to ride one instead of driving a car. Ultimately it doesn't really matter why someone wants to not take Sacred Hunt, the fact that the option is open to them is a good thing no matter their reason.<br /> <br /> And anyway, the strawman has a point. You <i>don't</i> need a car to travel between cities. A car makes it easier, but you absolutely can do it without a car.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048340#post1048340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would say is more similarly to being a serial diablerist. Yes, its a viable playstyle as long as either the whole group is into it or the player accepts the idea that when its becomes known he is gonna be dead. Quoting a documental on discovery channel &quot;Nobody likes a cannibal&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. That option should still be open to groups who want to play that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-13-2017, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T18:31:06-08:00","id":1048523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048311#post1048311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could say the same thing about &quot;someone needs to have dots in Survival so we can actually track prey - this time it's you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Case in point: none of the PCs in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/930212-ctl-water-under-the-bridge-2e-playtest-ap\">Water Under the Bridge</a> had any dots in Animal Ken for eighty percent of the current runtime despite the motley's nominal purpose being to help find a place for a bunch of rats to live in a Hedge full of territorial magical creatures and at least one of them actively eying Fang and Talon for the Perception booster. (Talking animals have spoiled them all. Especially Milton.)<br /> <br /> My protestations to the contrary notwithstanding, it hasn't done much to hamper their functioning, not least because \u2014 surprise, surprise \u2014 one of them has a Mentor who knows how to doggo and NPCs are a resource just as surely as anything on your own character sheet is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T19:07:49-08:00","id":1048534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1048375#post1048375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What werewolf would want to have a packmember who is a petty wannabe tyrant who tries to extort the rest of the pack? Specially when he is 2xp points away to be replaceable</div> </div> </div> </div> So, there's no middle ground? Diplomacy, tact, ability to leverage something at the right moment than using it as a blunt hammer? No one is recommending a petty tyrant. But using it correctly in the right time and place, and its a pretty effective move if you have the need for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:28:50-08:00","id":1050068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1047824#post1047824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understands now <i>why </i>Sacred Hunt is needed to be Rite in first place. <b>I still just thinks making it 2 dot one is rather illogical - it's the first Rite every one Uratha would learn, any time.</b> It's still a Rite, but invoked every time pack goes on Hunt - that is, almost every other day. Making it 'very specialized part of what you are you learn after monthes or even year of traning' ( as 2 dot idicate ) does not mesh with in setting material.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Ghost Wolf heartily disagrees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T09:54:52-08:00","id":1051033,"title":"","content":"In the games I run, Siskur-Dah is not a rite, but an innate part of being Uratha. For my group, the rite actually removed the feel of the shamanistic culture and made the Hunt less of an everyday part of your soul/life and more a tedious pause, or something that awkwardly interrupted the flow of scenes. There was also the OOC stress that not-taking the rite meant that you would lose out on potential XP from the condition which was a legit concern at my table.<br /> <br /> There's still a difference though between a hunt and The Sacred Hunt - but now there's no rolls required. The huntmaster declares their intent to the Shadow and the condition is given. My players still actively make up rites or dedicate screen time to announcing the hunt, even more so now that it feels more organically entwined in the setting for them. What I do have is that Sacred Hunts used frivolously, or abusively are equivalent to getting you and your pack blacklisted from the Shadow and other Uratha who do honor what the ancient way was. It's a really good way of getting Predator Kings declaring you Prey because you're disrespecting the law of the Shadow and your place within it.<br /> <br /> Sum Up: Sacred Hunt is a freebie non-rite thing that every wolfy gets, and practically nothing has changed save for new werewolves starting with rites that aren't Sacred Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T12:11:35-08:00","id":1051081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051033#post1051033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was also the OOC stress that not-taking the rite meant that you would lose out on potential XP from the condition which was a legit concern at my table.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bJust to be clear, in case there's a misconception here: Werewolves don't need to know the rite themselves to be able to receive the Siskur-Dah Condition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T12:35:47-08:00","id":1051102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051033#post1051033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the games I run, Siskur-Dah is not a rite, but an innate part of being Uratha. For my group, the rite actually removed the feel of the shamanistic culture and made the Hunt less of an everyday part of your soul/life and more a tedious pause, or something that awkwardly interrupted the flow of scenes. There was also the OOC stress that not-taking the rite meant that you would lose out on potential XP from the condition which was a legit concern at my table.<br /> <br /> There's still a difference though between a hunt and The Sacred Hunt - but now there's no rolls required. The huntmaster declares their intent to the Shadow and the condition is given. My players still actively make up rites or dedicate screen time to announcing the hunt, even more so now that it feels more organically entwined in the setting for them. What I do have is that Sacred Hunts used frivolously, or abusively are equivalent to getting you and your pack blacklisted from the Shadow and other Uratha who do honor what the ancient way was. It's a really good way of getting Predator Kings declaring you Prey because you're disrespecting the law of the Shadow and your place within it.<br /> <br /> Sum Up: Sacred Hunt is a freebie non-rite thing that every wolfy gets, and practically nothing has changed save for new werewolves starting with rites that aren't Sacred Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly how I treat it, but it's still a rite, still costs XP or &quot;freebies&quot;. One of the basic rules is &quot;if there's no risk of failure or stakes, don't roll.&quot; Taking 5 minutes to roll the sacred hunt every time gets old fast. I make a few descriptions on how we're honoring the hunt, how we're bloodying ourselves to link our purpose to the Totems and carry on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T13:52:08-08:00","id":1051133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051081#post1051081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bJust to be clear, in case there's a misconception here: Werewolves don't need to know the rite themselves to be able to receive the Siskur-Dah Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I run smaller games online and thus when there's only two to three PCs, there's this illusion of commitment to one of them taking Siskur-Dah as a rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T17:40:53-08:00","id":1051242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051033#post1051033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the games I run, Siskur-Dah is not a rite, but an innate part of being Uratha. For my group, the rite actually removed the feel of the shamanistic culture and made the Hunt less of an everyday part of your soul/life and more a tedious pause, or something that awkwardly interrupted the flow of scenes. There was also the OOC stress that not-taking the rite meant that you would lose out on potential XP from the condition which was a legit concern at my table.<br /> <br /> There's still a difference though between a hunt and The Sacred Hunt - but now there's no rolls required. The huntmaster declares their intent to the Shadow and the condition is given. My players still actively make up rites or dedicate screen time to announcing the hunt, even more so now that it feels more organically entwined in the setting for them. What I do have is that Sacred Hunts used frivolously, or abusively are equivalent to getting you and your pack blacklisted from the Shadow and other Uratha who do honor what the ancient way was. It's a really good way of getting Predator Kings declaring you Prey because you're disrespecting the law of the Shadow and your place within it.<br /> <br /> Sum Up: Sacred Hunt is a freebie non-rite thing that every wolfy gets, and practically nothing has changed save for new werewolves starting with rites that aren't Sacred Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, functionally, this is no different than giving your players 4 free dots of Rites, mandating that two of them be spent on Sacred Hunt, and following the good GMing practice of not calling for rolls when the results of the action are not uncertain or dramatically interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T18:54:59-08:00","id":1051285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051242#post1051242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, functionally, this is no different than giving your players 4 free dots of Rites, mandating that two of them be spent on Sacred Hunt, and following the good GMing practice of not calling for rolls when the results of the action are not uncertain or dramatically interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, we can go with the judgemental tone. Essentially, yes, and it's done absolutely nothing but make life at the table far more enjoyable for my players and myself.<br /> <br /> edit: And to re-stress this, it's purely a thing that I believe works for the group of players I have. I'm not in favor of my quirk becoming the norm, but for the style of play I do, and the themes I emphasize in Werewolf, it's the best solution we've come up with concerning merits at character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 02-18-2017, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T19:23:57-08:00","id":1051303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051285#post1051285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, we can go with the judgemental tone. Essentially, yes, and it's done absolutely nothing but make life at the table far more enjoyable for my players and myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, that was not an appropriate tone for me to use. I apologize, this topic seems to irritate me to and I shouldn't take that out on you, or other users. Thanks for calling me on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051285#post1051285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">edit: And to re-stress this, it's purely a thing that I believe works for the group of players I have. I'm not in favor of my quirk becoming the norm, but for the style of play I do, and the themes I emphasize in Werewolf, it's the best solution we've come up with concerning merits at character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. You do you. It just seems really strange to me that people are bothered by having the option to not take Sacred Hunt at character creation. No one would miss those two Rite dots if the writers had just given all werewolves Sacred Hunt free. But because they did it in a way that allows you to take something else of equal value if they don't want it, people who do want it feel cheated of the something else. Its bizarre to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T19:28:15-08:00","id":1051305,"title":"","content":"I also give every werewolf in my game Sacred Hunt for free. It has enhanced the quality of my games because every player has the opportunity to declare Siskur-Dah for something they are passionate about, and interject their own unique take on the Sacred Hunt ritual. As a result, I've seen a wider variety of Sacred Hunts, each tailored to the personal natures of the various characters leading these rituals.<br /> <br /> While this could technically be done by a ritemaster initiating the ritual then giving someone else leadership, giving everyone Sacred Hunt makes the process a little more personal to every character, easier to roleplay, and frees the ritemaster to take other rituals the pack might need. I've experienced no negatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T19:47:03-08:00","id":1051321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051303#post1051303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, that was not an appropriate tone for me to use. I apologize, this topic seems to irritate me to and I shouldn't take that out on you, or other users. Thanks for calling me on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I came back because I realized I was being snippy in my reply as well, so I apologize as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051303#post1051303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For sure. You do you. It just seems really strange to me that people are bothered by having the option to not take Sacred Hunt at character creation. No one would miss those two Rite dots if the writers had just given all werewolves Sacred Hunt free. But because they did it in a way that allows you to take something else of equal value if they don't want it, people who do want it feel cheated of the something else. Its bizarre to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I brought up the illusion of choice. For my players, that's actually an issue because Siskur-Dah has XP potential and a lot of it, and that removes the concept of equal value for the other rites. Banish is nice, but it doesn't reward you a beat per exceptional. In the end, that feeling of being cheated was something I didn't want to deal with, so I just added it in innately and it removes that one bit of stress.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T20:20:28-08:00","id":1051335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051321#post1051321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I came back because I realized I was being snippy in my reply as well, so I apologize as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're cool, no worries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051321#post1051321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I brought up the illusion of choice. For my players, that's actually an issue because Siskur-Dah has XP potential and a lot of it, and that removes the concept of equal value for the other rites. Banish is nice, but it doesn't reward you a beat per exceptional. In the end, that feeling of being cheated was something I didn't want to deal with, so I just added it in innately and it removes that one bit of stress.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's weird to me is that they feel cheated at all when you do offer that choice. <i>especially</i> if they view Sacred Hunt as being obviously more valuable than the other options. &quot;Why do I have to be the one to take Sacred Hunt?&quot; seems to be a weird complaint if you think Sacred Hunt is the best 2-dot Rie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T20:27:27-08:00","id":1051340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051305#post1051305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also give every werewolf in my game Sacred Hunt for free. It has enhanced the quality of my games because every player has the opportunity to declare Siskur-Dah for something they are passionate about, and interject their own unique take on the Sacred Hunt ritual. As a result, I've seen a wider variety of Sacred Hunts, each tailored to the personal natures of the various characters leading these rituals.<br /> <br /> While this could technically be done by a ritemaster initiating the ritual then giving someone else leadership, giving everyone Sacred Hunt makes the process a little more personal to every character, easier to roleplay, and frees the ritemaster to take other rituals the pack might need. I've experienced no negatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it could be done by everyone who wants to lead Siskur-Dah using their free Rite dots to take Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> I mean, I get that giving more free Rite dots doesn't have any negative side effects. Neither does giving more free Merit dots. But it's strange to me that people feel such a strong need to have a free 2-dot Rite <i>and</i> 2 free dots of Rites they can spend on whatever they want. I would bet dollars to doughnuts this complaint would not exist if the writers had given Sacred Hunt for free and 0 free Rite dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-18-2017, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T21:00:55-08:00","id":1051346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051340#post1051340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or it could be done by everyone who wants to lead Siskur-Dah using their free Rite dots to take Sacred Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly could be done that way, but all of my players agree that would be less fun than having 2 Ritual Dots to play around with. Besides, I personally feel that Werewolf has fewer thematic ties to hunting than Vampire does at this point, and giving everyone Sacred Hunt for free is a small step towards strengthening that theme. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051340#post1051340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I get that giving more free Rite dots doesn't have any negative side effects. Neither does giving more free Merit dots. But it's strange to me that people feel such a strong need to have a free 2-dot Rite <i>and</i> 2 free dots of Rites they can spend on whatever they want. I would bet dollars to doughnuts this complaint would not exist if the writers had given Sacred Hunt for free and 0 free Rite dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, it probably would not exist. But the same could be said for any MMO or game where something gets toned down -- nobody would get upset if those changes to the game had already been done before the game was launched/sold/whatever. It's just human nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T21:02:36-08:00","id":1051347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051321#post1051321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> because Siskur-Dah has XP potential and a lot of it, </div> </div> </div> </div>I think you missed what Acrozatarim said earlier. It doesn't matter who leads the Siskur-dah rite, everyone present gets the condition. So unless your packmates are spending all their time alone and never coming together to do things like sacred hunt, no one is missing out on the XP potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T21:14:11-08:00","id":1051352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051346#post1051346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right, it probably would not exist. But the same could be said for any MMO or game where something gets toned down -- nobody would get upset if those changes to the game had already been done before the game was launched/sold/whatever. It's just human nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't changed or toned down, though. The writers thought, hey, you know what would be cool? What if instead of just giving Sacred Hunt for free, we give people it's cost in free Rite dots. That way if anyone doesn't want it, they aren't forced to take it?&quot;<br /> <br /> They got complaints, for giving us <i>more</i> freedom in building our characters, because everyone wants to have their cake and eat it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T21:39:26-08:00","id":1051358,"title":"","content":"I just will sit and see how <b>Aynie</b> and <b>Iry</b> makes our arguments in polite way... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T21:46:48-08:00","id":1051362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051347#post1051347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you missed what Acrozatarim said earlier. It doesn't matter who leads the Siskur-dah rite, everyone present gets the condition. So unless your packmates are spending all their time alone and never coming together to do things like sacred hunt, no one is missing out on the XP potential.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I didn't miss it. In my bigger games with 4+ players, this wasn't an issue and I ran RAW.<br /> <br /> However with school and work I now run small games. 1 or 2 players at most, and the issue surrounds the fact that everyone has rites they want to take besides Siskur-Dah, with merits being devoured incredibly fast before the consideration of rites; and whoever takes the Siskur-Dah devolves into who has the best tribe for the Hunt and it just further devolved into an unpleasant course of issues. People felt forced to either have everyone pick it up so they'd have the best tribal bonuses represented or one person pick it up at first and lose out on the rites they might have wanted instead.<br /> <br /> The last Siskur-Dah we ran, it added a whopping 15 extra beats over the course of three sessions - and that's on top of my end game hand out of about 4-5 beats. That's why my players feel like it has to be picked up by someone, and the grumblings that caused - even benign and small as they were were grumblings I didn't want to deal with.<br /> <br /> I actually think Siskur-Dah is pretty damn powerful for only a 2-dot rite, and it's insane to not pop it for nearly every embodiment of a hunt but that's not the point of the current discussion.<br /> <br /> edit: Yes, I know the 15 beats is an incredible outlier, our average is about 4 extra per Siskur-Dah, which is what makes it sooooo good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 02-19-2017, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T21:59:43-08:00","id":1051365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051346#post1051346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, I personally feel that Werewolf has fewer thematic ties to hunting than Vampire does at this point, and giving everyone Sacred Hunt for free is a small step towards strengthening that theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also \u2014 and this really can't be stressed enough \u2014 a starting character that still has a spiritual Touchstone and hasn't dumped literally all of their Merit dots into Primal Urge takes three months of neglecting the Sacred Hunt before they start suffering the consequences, and the consequences are\u2026<br /> <br /> Losing a point of Essence per day (which, unlike with vampires, doesn't translate to any extra consequences besides lack of magical fuel until the outermost extremes of the species' feeding restrictions)\u2026<br /> <br /> Rolling Resolve + Composure with a null modifier to avoid slipping once per day, and\u2026<br /> <br /> Will begin having a much worse time of things once they (eventually) rise to Harmony 8 (at which point the penalty from higher Harmony rises above the default Touchstone bonus and the spiritual Touchstone detaches), whereupon\u2026<br /> <br /> They begin to rapidly get less wiggle room for their personal Death Rage trigger (which nevertheless does not reach the extremes of Passive triggers until Harmony 10) to kick off a stretch of gambling Resolve + Composure for an exceptional success (which can be converted to aiming for five turns of lucidity with a one-dot rite that only mandates a single unassisted roll per month) to stop a ten-minute killfrenzy, many of which can be avoided by a Ghost Wolf. Also\u2026<br /> <br /> They gain an expanded list of breaking points toward Spirit, including several things that Death Rage all but gives them for free with the caveat of needing to find out about them later, some of which also give them Essence.<br /> <br /> If they still have their physical Touchstone, they can pretty much always jump their way back from Harmony 10, whereupon they only need to get to a locus and succeed once on a roll of three or more dice before they start rolling a counteractive breaking point every day until they either break back down to Harmony 7 and can start rebalancing or (at least implicitly) drop back into the Flesh at Harmony 10, whereupon the pressure to kill and eat people is higher but the primary impetus is still the (theoretically avoidable or at least manageable) personal triggers.<br /> <br /> It's a lifestyle that's evidently not desirable to a lot of Uratha, but it's clearly <i>playable</i>, particularly given that &quot;increase the bonus your spiritual Touchstone provides&quot; is a fairly cheap Merit, as is &quot;make getting out of soft-Rage easier.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-19-2017, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T22:14:13-08:00","id":1051371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051362#post1051362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last Siskur-Dah we ran, it added a whopping 15 extra beats over the course of three sessions - and that's on top of my end game hand out of about 4-5 beats. That's why my players feel like it has to be picked up by someone, and the grumblings that caused - even benign and small as they were were grumblings I didn't want to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>So (and no snark at you), players want the 15-odd extra beats but don't want to invest their <b>free</b> rites dots into the thing that generates those extra beats, because they want other stuff?<br /> <br /> Yep, sounds like players.<br /> <br /> (Personally, I would have told them to STFU and buy the extra rites from their 15ish extra beats per hunt.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T22:17:22-08:00","id":1051372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051352#post1051352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't changed or toned down, though. The writers thought, hey, you know what would be cool? What if instead of just giving Sacred Hunt for free, we give people it's cost in free Rite dots. That way if anyone doesn't want it, they aren't forced to take it?&quot;<br /> <br /> They got complaints, for giving us <i>more</i> freedom in building our characters, because everyone wants to have their cake and eat it too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly think it would have been a better design decision to give Sacred Hunt for free in addition to 2 Ritual Dots, as opposed to the way they decided to do it. Both options are plenty of fun, with my subjective opinion that one is slightly more fun for players than the other. But there was nothing wrong with the choice they settled on. Especially because anybody who prefers it the other way can easily do so in their own games (as myself and others have done).<br /> <br /> And it's only natural for everyone to want their cake and eat it too! I wouldn't want a cake I couldn't eat; I would be salivating all over the place. Hehehe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T22:22:12-08:00","id":1051374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051371#post1051371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So (and no snark at you), players want the 15-odd extra beats but don't want to invest their <b>free</b> rites dots into the thing that generates those extra beats, because they want other stuff?<br /> <br /> Yep, sounds like players.<br /> <br /> (Personally, I would have told them to STFU and buy the extra rites from their 15ish extra beats per hunt.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. They're players but ultimately just adding it innately was the better option because they're usually throwing that extra XP at things to stave off my eventual murder of them and everything they love. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also because I have to see them outside of games. And hilariously this entire thing comes down to a simple two extra XP, or an average of two games with or without the rite.<br /> <br /> In larger games, I have absolutely no qualms keeping RAW but with the smaller games, where there's more character focus and they're spending XP on NPCs and world-development that will ultimately see a lot more screen time due to the simple nature of having more time overall to do so, I went with innate.<br /> <br /> And alas, Wyrd, why I chose to do it has nothing to do with the reasons you want to swap it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 02-19-2017, 01:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T22:27:09-08:00","id":1051375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051372#post1051372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly think it would have been a better design decision to give Sacred Hunt for free in addition to 2 Ritual Dots,</div> </div> </div> </div>This was never an option. It's between Sacred Hunt and 0 free Rite dots, or 2 free Rite dots with which you can buy Sacred Hunt if you want it. The option they chose is the better design choice in my opinion because it provides more flexibility. Free Sacred Hunt and 2 free Rite dots is something players made up because they wanted to have Sacred Hunt and have the dots the writers gave us to buy it with. It's like complaining that you can't start with Primal Urge 3 <i>and</i> ten Merit dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051372#post1051372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's only natural for everyone to want their cake and eat it too! I wouldn't want a cake I couldn't eat; I would be salivating all over the place. Hehehe.</div> </div> </div> </div>But once you <i>eat</i> the cake, you no longer <i>have</i> a cake. Because it's been eaten. In this analogy Sacred Hunt is the experience of eating cake and the two free Rite dots are a cake. The players want the experience of eating cake but they want the cake to still be there after they have experienced eating it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-19-2017, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T22:36:34-08:00","id":1051378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051372#post1051372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly think it would have been a better design decision to give Sacred Hunt for free in addition to 2 Ritual Dots</div> </div> </div> </div>There should always be the option for a player to choose to not take Sacred Hunt. Many stories require and support that choice.<br /> <br /> Characters do have incentive to take <i>Siskur-Dah</i>. That's why we made it so that everyone has the chance to take it, for free, at character creation. We also made it so that players who chose to not take it, for whatever reason, weren't disadvantaged and could take something else of equal value.<br /> <br /> And we did that because we didn't want groups to have to have a 'designated ritemaster' who was forced to spend her points on all the things that enable the pack but other whiny players don't want to take because of all the (IMO) bullshit reasons above.<br /> <br /> I still don't think the Sacred Hunt rite should be a Luna-given thing that every werewolf starts with. That shuts down player choice, and requires the Storyteller to take something away from players to run those games. (Even if she replaces it with something else, they've had choice taken from them.)<br /> <br /> And I certainly disagree with you that it would have been a better design decision. Mostly because the people who are arguing for it (with all due respect to each of them) are thinking at the micro level of 'my game table' and 'other game tables are like mine', when we're trying to think beyond that to the macro level of 'what gives most choice to as many game styles as possible'.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T22:38:35-08:00","id":1051379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051374#post1051374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And alas, Wyrd, why I chose to do it has nothing to do with the reasons you want to swap it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you pointed the same things as I, so I will disagree with your pruning our camp - we both want the same things - <i><b>do not</b> want players to quarrel</i> <i>over who takes Sacred Hunt on chargen</i>. I only pointed next argument for that - 'Our ritemaster is dead/greavely wounded'. But with most spirits being able to teach Sacred Hunt in play ( when ritemaster is wounded ) solving this particular one, it's still only problem of raising unnecessary squabbles with players at chargen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-19-2017, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T22:47:39-08:00","id":1051380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051375#post1051375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was never an option. It's between Sacred Hunt and 0 free Rite dots, or 2 free Rite dots with which you can buy Sacred Hunt if you want it. The option they chose is the better design choice in my opinion because it provides more flexibility. Free Sacred Hunt and 2 free Rite dots is something players made up because they wanted to have Sacred Hunt and have the dots the writers gave us to buy it with. It's like complaining that you can't start with Primal Urge 3 <i>and</i> ten Merit dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it was always an option, short of Rich himself descending upon the developers and declaring &quot;Thou shall not allow Sacred Hunt and 2 Ritual Dots!&quot; The free Ritual Dots themselves are an incentive for players to give the Ritual system a try; to dip their proverbial toe into the waters of ritual mechanics and see how they like it. Once again, at no point in this am I saying the choice they made was bad. 2 Ritual Dots with the option to buy Sacred Hunt is certainly better, in my opinion, than 0 Ritual Dots and mandatory Sacred Hunt. But there was always the third option of 2 Ritual Dots <i><b>AND</b></i> Sacred Hunt, which would have been the better design decision out of the three (IMHO, naturally).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051375#post1051375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But once you <i>eat</i> the cake, you no longer <i>have</i> a cake. Because it's been eaten. In this analogy Sacred Hunt is the experience of eating cake and the two free Rite dots are a cake. The players want the experience of eating cake but they don't want to not have a cake anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds fine to me! Let them both eat the cake <i><b>AND</b></i> have the cake simultaneously! More fun for everyone without any considerable impacts to balance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T23:09:39-08:00","id":1051385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051380#post1051380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it was always an option, short of Rich himself descending upon the developers and declaring &quot;Thou shall not allow Sacred Hunt and 2 Ritual Dots!&quot; The free Ritual Dots themselves are an incentive for players to give the Ritual system a try; to dip their proverbial toe into the waters of ritual mechanics and see how they like it. Once again, at no point in this am I saying the choice they made was bad. 2 Ritual Dots with the option to buy Sacred Hunt is certainly better, in my opinion, than 0 Ritual Dots and mandatory Sacred Hunt. <b>But there was always the third option of 2 Ritual Dots <i><b>AND</b></i> Sacred Hunt, which would have been the better design decision out of the three (IMHO, naturally</b>).</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely my POV! And for having characters without Sacred Hunt in on 'free Sacred Hunt and 2 dots of Rites Trait' option - just mark that freshly First Changed and Ghost Wolves do <b>not</b> have Sacred Hunt and Tribes teach each member of Scared Hunt on <i>their initiation</i> to the Tribe. You want to run stories of Tribes members without Scared Hunt? Just point they did not learned yet as their initiation. I.E. The same way <i>High Speech</i> Merit for Orders was treated in <b>Mage</b> 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T23:16:33-08:00","id":1051389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051378#post1051378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should always be the option for a player to choose to not take Sacred Hunt. Many stories require and support that choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>That option is always available to the player, simply by the player talking with the storyteller and asking not to have that ability. Exactly the same way a player could ask their storyteller if their character could be unable to take Hishu or Dalu for some compelling character reason (or something similar).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051378#post1051378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Characters do have incentive to take <i>Siskur-Dah</i>. That's why we made it so that everyone has the chance to take it, for free, at character creation. We also made it so that players who chose to not take it, for whatever reason, weren't disadvantaged and could take something else of equal value.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh certainly. The incentives to take Sacred Hunt are so impressive, and so great, that it would be almost silly not to take it. Which essentially transforms the option into a nearly mandatory tax for... at least one person in the pack. Not <i>actually</i> mandatory, of course, but almost unheard of for nobody to take it. Somewhat similar to the way that certain feats in D&amp;D became nearly mandatory, because of the way that they were so beneficial almost everyone took them (only one person in this case). Or any other game where one option gives a considerably larger benefit than many other options.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051378#post1051378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't think the Sacred Hunt rite should be a Luna-given thing that every werewolf starts with. That shuts down player choice, and requires the Storyteller to take something away from players to run those games. (Even if she replaces it with something else, they've had choice taken from them.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have created a red herring here. Having Sacred Hunt be free only takes away player choice in the same way that being able to shapeshift takes away player choice, or naturally healing bashing damage takes away player choice, or playing a werewolf or wolfblooded in general takes away player choice. Which is to say, you are choosing to play a particular splat -- with it comes a series of benefits and complications. Among those are X, and you are free to negotiate with your storyteller to have less than X if you can come up with a compelling reason for it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051378#post1051378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I certainly disagree with you that it would have been a better design decision. Mostly because the people who are arguing for it (with all due respect to each of them) are thinking at the micro level of 'my game table' and 'other game tables are like mine', when we're trying to think beyond that to the macro level of 'what gives most choice to as many game styles as possible'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I definitely want to be clear that I am speaking about the macro level of 'what gives the most choice to as many game styles as possible'. But it is perfectly fine for us to agree to disagree. It just means we have slightly different ideals about game design philosophy and balance, and neither of those opinions are bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 02-19-2017, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T23:22:04-08:00","id":1051391,"title":"","content":"I on the other hand just chimed in with micro-level musings, mostly because my players are fussy cats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T23:41:11-08:00","id":1051394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051380#post1051380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it was always an option, short of Rich himself descending upon the developers and declaring &quot;Thou shall not allow Sacred Hunt and 2 Ritual Dots!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish these forums had an eye-rolling emoji. You know what I meant. It was never an option the writers considered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051380#post1051380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The free Ritual Dots themselves are an incentive for players to give the Ritual system a try; to dip their proverbial toe into the waters of ritual mechanics and see how they like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're not. A writer is literally telling you in this very thread that they were written as a way to give players who want Sacred Hunt the ability to start the game with it for free, and to give players who don't want Sacred Hunt the ability to start the game without it and not be at an effective -2 experience compared to the players who did want to start with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051380#post1051380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, at no point in this am I saying the choice they made was bad. 2 Ritual Dots with the option to buy Sacred Hunt is certainly better, in my opinion, than 0 Ritual Dots and mandatory Sacred Hunt. But there was always the third option of 2 Ritual Dots <i><b>AND</b></i> Sacred Hunt, which would have been the better design decision out of the three (IMHO, naturally).</div> </div> </div> </div>Follow that train of thought to its last stop. If two free Rite dots is a better option than 0 free Rite dots and mandatory Sacred Hunt, then surely 4 free Rite dots is better than 2 free Rite dots and mandatory Sacred Hunt. And now we're back to players complaining that they have to spend half of their starting Rite dots if they want Sacred Hunt. Do we then conclude that it would have been better for the writers to give starting characters 4 free Rite dots <i>and</i> Sacred Hunt? But then, surely 6 free Rite dots would be better even than that. Etcetera, etcetera, etcetera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-19-2017, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T23:44:12-08:00","id":1051395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051389#post1051389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh certainly. The incentives to take Sacred Hunt are so impressive, and so great, that it would be almost silly not to take it. Which essentially transforms the option into a nearly mandatory tax for... at least one person in the pack. Not <i>actually</i> mandatory, of course, but almost unheard of for nobody to take it. Somewhat similar to the way that certain feats in D&amp;D became nearly mandatory, because of the way that they were so beneficial almost everyone took them. Or any other game where one option gives a considerably larger benefit than many other options.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference, at least in Feats, is that the rite is offered freely at character creation, and can be bought at any time later. It can even be used through a mentor, though he might tire of using the rite on your pack. It's something they can seek out in-game without anyone having to write 'Sacred Hunt' in their list of rites. Rites are not something you can get every other level and max out at a certain point and can never get another again. The Sacred Hunt is always potentially available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you have created a red herring here. Having Sacred Hunt be free only takes away player choice in the same way that being able to shapeshift takes away player choice, or naturally healing bashing damage takes away player choice, or playing a werewolf or wolfblooded in general takes away player choice. Which is to say, you are choosing to play a particular splat -- with it comes a series of benefits and complications. Among those are X, and you are free to negotiate with your storyteller to have less than X if you can come up with a compelling reason for it. </div> </div> </div>Having Sacred Hunt be free and forced eliminates any option of having the character who just doesn't know. Who has not been exposed to the greater society of werewolves and does not know what they are. Who is Forsaken. And the setting has that as a prominent option.<br /> <br /> Instead, it's offered with free rite dots. Take it, or don't. You can have an oblivious, lost character, a character sure in their ability to get access to it in the world, or a character who can fend for themselves.<br /> <br /> I mean, this is the entire point of the toolbox approach. You can adjust your games accordingly, as people in this forum have. But it offers a playstyle with more options that fit the designed setting, and lets you subtract or add from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-19-2017, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T00:05:09-08:00","id":1051397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051394#post1051394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish these forums had an eye-rolling emoji. You know what I meant. It was never an option the writers considered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be mistaken, but based on what I am reading from Bunyip, they did consider it and rejected it because it did not match their game design philosophy. And there's nothing wrong with that, because we're just talking about opinions in the first place. =P<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051394#post1051394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they're not. A writer is literally telling you in this very thread that they were written as a way to give players who want Sacred Hunt the ability to start the game with it for free, and to give players who don't want Sacred Hunt the ability to start the game without it and not be at an effective -2 experience compared to the players who did want to start with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly cannot read their mind; I was merely speaking about what I would have done as a game developer, and the thought process that would normally go into such a decision.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051394#post1051394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Follow that train of thought to its last stop. If two free Rite dots is a better option than 0 free Rite dots and mandatory Sacred Hunt, then surely 4 free Rite dots is better than 2 free Rite dots and mandatory Sacred Hunt. And now we're back to players complaining that they have to spend half of their starting Rite dots if they want Sacred Hunt. Do we then conclude that it would have been better for the writers to give starting characters 4 free Rite dots <i>and</i> Sacred Hunt? But then, surely 6 free Rite dots would be better even than that. Etcetera, etcetera, etcetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. The more free Ritual Dots that are being given to the player, the more it creates certain balance implications. Those implications might be relatively minor at the start, but we can't follow that train of thought to its 'last stop' without ending up considerably heavy on one side of the balance equation. 2 Dots is a relatively harmless way to allow players to dabble with the ritual system. I daresay the system could withstand going up to 4 before things start getting somewhat wobbly, but it's not a decision I would make.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051395#post1051395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference, at least in Feats, is that the rite is offered freely at character creation, and can be bought at any time later. It can even be used through a mentor, though he might tire of using the rite on your pack. It's something they can seek out in-game without anyone having to write 'Sacred Hunt' in their list of rites. Rites are not something you can get every other level and max out at a certain point and can never get another again. The Sacred Hunt is always potentially available.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately we're not talking about something major here. Sacred Hunt is certainly extremely enticing, and will frequently pay for itself in just a handful of games. But it's only 2 XP away for any character that wants to take it. It's just our opinion that giving it to every werewolf character creates a greater number of options, and a greater amount of fun than the current system. And it's okay to have that opinion, just like it's okay to have the opinion that the system is fine the way it is.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051395#post1051395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having Sacred Hunt be free and forced eliminates any option of having the character who just doesn't know. Who has not been exposed to the greater society of werewolves and does not know what they are. Who is Forsaken. And the setting has that as a prominent option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely disagree for the same reason I disagreed with Bunyip. Having Sacred Hunt be free cannot stop a player from deciding that her character just doesn't know how to do it. Who has not been exposed to the greater society of werewolves and does not know what they are. Or who is Forsaken. It's always an option to ignore a mechanic that doesn't force you to take an action, or ask the storyteller if your character could simply not know it. I'm just certain (IMHO, once again) that giving it to everyone adds more options, instead of less options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 02-19-2017, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T00:25:47-08:00","id":1051400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051397#post1051397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately we're not talking about something major here. Sacred Hunt is certainly extremely enticing, and will frequently pay for itself in just a handful of games. But it's only 2 XP away for any character that wants to take it. It's just our opinion that giving it to every werewolf character creates a greater number of options, and a greater amount of fun than the current system. And it's okay to have that opinion, just like it's okay to have the opinion that the system is fine the way it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just said 'The incentives to take Sacred Hunt are so impressive, and so great, that it would be almost silly not to take it.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I definitely disagree for the same reason I disagreed with Bunyip. Having Sacred Hunt be free cannot stop a player from deciding that her character just doesn't know how to do it. Who has not been exposed to the greater society of werewolves and does not know what they are. Or who is Forsaken. It's always an option to ignore a mechanic that doesn't force you to take an action, or ask the storyteller if your character could simply not know it. I'm just certain (IMHO, once again) that giving it to everyone adds more options, instead of less options. </div> </div> </div>Could you name some of these options? Because so far you've closed off one angle of play, without storyteller permission, and you've taken away wyrdhamsters storyline, and forced everyone to being a ritemaster.<br /> <br /> The only option presented in this is characters being able to get rites, which is an option in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T00:26:01-08:00","id":1051401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051397#post1051397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just certain (IMHO, once again) that giving it to everyone adds more options, instead of less options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a notion: Do what Beast does with the starting Lair Chamber.<br /> <br /> From one perspective, a starting Beast character can choose to begin the game without having established one of their Lair's two Chambers (the second being the universally-required Heart) and gain two free Experiences instead.<br /> <br /> From another perspective, a starting Beast character begins the game with two free Experiences, which they may spend at character creation to have already established one of their Lair's Chambers outside the Heart.<br /> <br /> By a similar token:<br /> <br /> From one perspective, a starting Werewolf character begins the game with two free dots of Rites (in addition to any they spend their starting Merit dots on), which they may spend at character creation to already know the Sacred Hunt ritual.<br /> <br /> From another perspective, a starting Werewolf character can choose to begin the game without having personally learned the underlying symbols of the Sacred Hunt ritual and gain two free dots of Rites instead.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of framing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T00:46:10-08:00","id":1051405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051400#post1051400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just said 'The incentives to take Sacred Hunt are so impressive, and so great, that it would be almost silly not to take it.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. 2XP is not a major expense to most players (though it will be to some).<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051400#post1051400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you name some of these options? Because so far you've closed off one angle of play, without storyteller permission, and you've taken away wyrdhamsters storyline, and forced everyone to being a ritemaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you explain this part of your post a little bit more? No angles of play have been closed off, I'm not sure what you mean by 'without storyteller permission, or how I have taken away Wyrdhamster's storyline, or forced everyone into being a ritemaster (that's already RAW).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T01:09:47-08:00","id":1051412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051405#post1051405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you explain this part of your post a little bit more?</div> </div> </div> </div>Making Sacred Hunt innate explicitly gates games without the rite behind the wall of subtractive fiat \u2014 effectively mandating houserules to run a story where characters have their tribal initiations but lack the mystical fundamentals to call the hunt on their own.<br /> <br /> i.e. &quot;without Storyteller permission, that angle of play is closed off.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T01:21:18-08:00","id":1051416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051412#post1051412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making Sacred Hunt innate explicitly gates games without the rite behind the wall of subtractive fiat \u2014 effectively mandating houserules to run a story where characters have their tribal initiations but lack the mystical fundamentals to call the hunt on their own.<br /> <br /> i.e. &quot;without Storyteller permission, that angle of play is closed off.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If the entire game doesn't have the rite, then everything remains equal because nobody has Sacred Hunt. Either way, everything is already behind the wall of fiat, where players need Storyteller permission for any portion of their character (especially backstory). Generally, it shouldn't be an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T06:50:18-08:00","id":1051494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051416#post1051416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, everything is already behind the wall of fiat, where players need Storyteller permission for any portion of their character (especially backstory).</div> </div> </div> </div>Elements of a character that the base rules as written do not allow tend to be weighted more heavily in this hobby where a substantial number of groups aren't comfortable stepping outside of printed material even when that's explicitly something the game expects and encourages them to do, and changes that would require un-publishing printed material to be made official are markedly less easily-implemented in that context than purely additive changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T07:29:33-08:00","id":1051513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051494#post1051494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elements of a character that the base rules as written do not allow tend to be weighted more heavily in this hobby where a substantial number of groups aren't comfortable stepping outside of printed material even when that's explicitly something the game expects and encourages them to do, and changes that would require un-publishing printed material to be made official are markedly less easily-implemented in that context than purely additive changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with what you are saying in a general sense, but this is not one of those situations. You don't technically need storyteller permission for your character to be 'ignorant' of something that doesn't force you to use it. This is not even something particularly radical like &quot;I do my best to avoid ever using Urhan&quot;. You could go an entire game never drawing attention to the fact that your character has no idea how to do the Sacred Hunt, the same way you could go an entire game never drawing attention to the fact that your character has no idea how to read.<br /> <br /> But we're not here to hide things from the storyteller, that was just being technical. Asking your storyteller if you can play a character who is ignorant of her heritage (and abstaining from activities like the Sacred Hunt on a player level) is no more or less likely to be rejected by your storyteller than someone who wants to play a foreigner, someone missing an eye, someone who wants to play a ghost wolf, or any other straightforward almost always approved thing (as long as you are not being disruptive at the table, as is the case with anything).<br /> <br /> Of course, there will always be a few storytellers who have very specific visions for their stories and might say no. But those storytellers could just as easily ask that nobody play a Blood Talon, that everyone be raised as a child soldier, or any number of other things that technically narrow your choices down but contribute to telling a hopefully interesting story. Not ever character we dream up fits perfectly into every game, and that's okay too (as long as everyone is having fun and knew about it up front).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T17:37:20-08:00","id":1051775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051513#post1051513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with what you are saying in a general sense, but this is not one of those situations. You don't technically need storyteller permission for your character to be 'ignorant' of something that doesn't force you to use it. This is not even something particularly radical like &quot;I do my best to avoid ever using Urhan&quot;. You could go an entire game never drawing attention to the fact that your character has no idea how to do the Sacred Hunt, the same way you could go an entire game never drawing attention to the fact that your character has no idea how to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a GM, player, and freelancer I get rather annoyed anytime people suggest I should just pretend my character doesn't have abilities he has because the designers think everyone should play a certain playstyle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T19:00:30-08:00","id":1051802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051775#post1051775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a GM, player, and freelancer I get rather annoyed anytime people suggest I should just pretend my character doesn't have abilities he has because the designers think everyone should play a certain playstyle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having the option to pretend your character doesn't have abilities increases the number of character concepts you can potentially play. The illiterate, the foreigner, the handicapped, the ghost wolf, the cub, etc. The ghost wolf even has mechanical support for it's missing abilities, which is very cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T19:48:16-08:00","id":1051817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051802#post1051802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having the option to pretend your character doesn't have abilities increases the number of character concepts you can potentially play. The illiterate, the foreigner, the handicapped, the ghost wolf, the cub, etc. The ghost wolf even has mechanical support for it's missing abilities, which is very cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except ghost wolf isn't pretending to be missing abilities, it is actually missing the abilities. It has actual text in the game saying how they work in the setting and the mechanics of the game. And those other things would be covered by conditions and simply not putting points into things or just saying your illiterate because there is no mechanics which govern literacy.<br /> <br /> What you're proposing reduces the amount of narratives possible in the game without using houserules and homebrew, which is innately negative to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T20:07:09-08:00","id":1051825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051817#post1051817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except ghost wolf isn't pretending to be missing abilities, it is actually missing the abilities. It has actual text in the game saying how they work in the setting and the mechanics of the game. And those other things would be covered by conditions and simply not putting points into things or just saying your illiterate because there is no mechanics which govern literacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a storyteller, you definitely have the power to make those things a reality in your own game! You can even create versions and bring them to the forums for discussion. I would love to see them, and think that would be a lot of fun.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051817#post1051817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're proposing reduces the amount of narratives possible in the game without using houserules and homebrew, which is innately negative to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>We will have to agree to disagree. But the important thing is that you do whatever you think is best for your own games, and your players. The great thing about the toolbox approach used by Chronicles of Darkness is that we can both have our way, and have tons of fun doing it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T20:32:54-08:00","id":1051834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051825#post1051825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a storyteller, you definitely have the power to make those things a reality in your own game! You can even create versions and bring them to the forums for discussion. I would love to see them, and think that would be a lot of fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except I don't need to do anything to make those a reality in my own game. With your thing, I do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We will have to agree to disagree. But the important thing is that you do whatever you think is best for your own games, and your players. The great thing about the toolbox approach used by Chronicles of Darkness is that we can both have our way, and have tons of fun doing it. </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about from a game design viewpoint, not a &quot;my game so I can make change anything, including saying everyone's a pony or that the moon is cheese&quot; viewpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T22:30:14-08:00","id":1051863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051834#post1051834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except I don't need to do anything to make those a reality in my own game. With your thing, I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not anything more than what you would normally communicate with your storyteller about, except in cases where the storyteller has a very specific vision they are trying to pursue.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051834#post1051834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking about from a game design viewpoint, not a &quot;my game so I can make change anything, including saying everyone's a pony or that the moon is cheese&quot; viewpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a game design perspective, allowing Sacred Hunt AND 2 Ritual Dots adds a small number of additional character choices, and a small amount of additional fun for the majority of players, with almost negligible impact to game balance (as always, IMHO). A favorable change!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T22:37:11-08:00","id":1051867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051863#post1051863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not anything more than what you would normally communicate with your storyteller about, except in cases where the storyteller has a very specific vision they are trying to pursue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering I play without houserules. It'd be over 100% more than I normally would communicate actually. You know that you don't need to use houserules to play CofD? :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From a game design perspective, allowing Sacred Hunt AND 2 Ritual Dots adds a small number of additional character choices, and a small amount of additional fun for the majority of players, with almost negligible impact to game balance (as always, IMHO). A favorable change! </div> </div> </div>It doesn't add any Character Choices, it increases the amount of rites werewolf characters starts with. It basically is &quot;treat your werewolf as if he had 2 extra XP, but I'm not letting you pick what that XP goes to&quot;. Werewolves with additional stuff at character creation are already in the rules by giving the werewolf extra XP, while removing the option for characters without the rite which many will probably never want or use in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T23:12:31-08:00","id":1051871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051867#post1051867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering I play without houserules. It'd be over 100% more than I normally would communicate actually. You know that you don't need to use houserules to play CofD? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Does your character have a backstory? Does your character have Allies, Mentors, or any of the social merits that require you to establish things and come to an agreement with your storyteller? Then that's the same amount of interaction that it would take establish that your character doesn't know how to do a Sacred Hunt. In other words, just the basic routine you already go through when creating a character.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051867#post1051867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't add any Character Choices, it increases the amount of rites werewolf characters starts with. It basically is &quot;treat your werewolf as if he had 2 extra XP, but I'm not letting you pick what that XP goes to&quot;. Werewolves with additional stuff at character creation are already in the rules by giving the werewolf extra XP, while removing the option for characters without the rite which many will probably never want or use in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, we will have to agree to disagree. I firmly stand by the opinion that making Sacred Hunt an innate ability of Werewolves adds character choices, encourages a little more roleplay, makes the Sacred Hunt a little more personal, and slightly adds to the theme &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T23:45:00-08:00","id":1051875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051871#post1051871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I firmly stand by the opinion that making Sacred Hunt an innate ability of Werewolves adds character choices, encourages a little more roleplay, makes the Sacred Hunt a little more personal, and slightly adds to the theme &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also makes it <i>not a rite.</i> A major part of the point of it being a rite and doing what it does is that it helps explain the substantial differences between the Forsaken and what many people in the modern Western world think of when the word &quot;werewolf&quot; comes up by providing a pervasive ritual element of Uratha society that allows them to better manage their time and Harmony.<br /> <br /> Making this feature innate does not make creating a character who somehow can't use it equivalent to starting with Social Merits. It makes it equivalent to me having to cobble together a Persistent Condition for one of my players because he took three dots in Socialize and wants to play a fish-out-of-water who regularly commits faux-pas in everyday mortal society \u2014 and that specific character at least has the excuse of being expressly conceived as woefully unintelligent, which is not a brush I imagine you want to tar every would-be Ghost Wolf with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T23:59:38-08:00","id":1051880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051875#post1051875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also makes it <i>not a rite.</i> A major part of the point of it being a rite and doing what it does is that it helps explain the substantial differences between the Forsaken and what many people in the modern Western world think of when the word &quot;werewolf&quot; comes up by providing a pervasive ritual element of Uratha society that allows them to better manage their time and Harmony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having 2 Ritual Dots in addition to possessing an innate ability to perform the Sacred Hunt accomplishes that goal admirably.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051875#post1051875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making this feature innate does not make creating a character who somehow can't use it equivalent to starting with Social Merits. It makes it equivalent to me having to cobble together a Persistent Condition for one of my players because he took three dots in Socialize and wants to play a fish-out-of-water who regularly commits faux-pas in everyday mortal society \u2014 and that specific character at least has the excuse of being expressly conceived as woefully unintelligent, which is not a brush I imagine you want to tar every would-be Ghost Wolf with.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are multiple solutions available to represent any character concept your players may want to embrace, and choosing to make a Persistent Condition for that character is certainly one of the options in your tool belt, but there is no need to make it complex if you are concerned about it. The player can simply not use Sacred Hunt and the game will be absolutely fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 02-20-2017, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T00:05:03-08:00","id":1051883,"title":"","content":"I will disagree that making Sacred Hunt 'free' is making it <i>not</i> Rite. If it's need ritual to activate, based on the connection to Shadow Realm and it's laws and must be invoked each time by performing it - it's <i>still</i> Rite. It's just one that PCs get for free in introduction to Tribes. For examples Ghost Wolves still would not have it simply for free - they would need to learn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-20-2017, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T01:31:10-08:00","id":1051896,"title":"","content":"I really don't get the problem. I have a Werewolf group for two years now and out of the four characters only one has Sacred Hunt and it is working perfectly fine. If you want to have a group where everybody has it but also want the players to have an additional rite, well just give Sacred Hunt to them for free and you are done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T06:56:26-08:00","id":1051984,"title":"","content":"The problem is that we're not allowed to have nice things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T07:47:21-08:00","id":1052002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051875#post1051875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also makes it <i>not a rite.</i> A major part of the point of it being a rite and doing what it does is that it helps explain the substantial differences between the Forsaken and what many people in the modern Western world think of when the word &quot;werewolf&quot; comes up by providing a pervasive ritual element of Uratha society that allows them to better manage their time and Harmony.<br /> <br /> Making this feature innate does not make creating a character who somehow can't use it equivalent to starting with Social Merits. It makes it equivalent to me having to cobble together a Persistent Condition for one of my players because he took three dots in Socialize and wants to play a fish-out-of-water who regularly commits faux-pas in everyday mortal society \u2014 and that specific character at least has the excuse of being expressly conceived as woefully unintelligent, which is not a brush I imagine you want to tar every would-be Ghost Wolf with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, it's still a rite for my group, and you have to be a part of a tribe to get the tribe's benefits. It's just 'free' at character creation. But I think there's a lot of defensiveness on both sides of this issue, and a glaring problem of &quot;You're running the game bad-wrong&quot; which ... is something we should stifle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T11:39:35-08:00","id":1052070,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. I definitely recommend people give it a try in their own games and see how they like it. It's not going to be for everyone, but I genuinely think it will add a little bit of extra fun and roleplaying for the majority of players out there. And there's nothing bad-wrong about running things the way they are now; the writers did a great job making a very fun game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:11:52-08:00","id":1052094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1052002#post1052002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, it's still a rite for my group, and you have to be a part of a tribe to get the tribe's benefits. It's just 'free' at character creation. But I think there's a lot of defensiveness on both sides of this issue, and a glaring problem of &quot;You're running the game bad-wrong&quot; which ... is something we should stifle.</div> </div> </div> </div>There might be less defensiveness if you didn't respond to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> who was replying to someone that was saying they made Sacred Hunt not-a-rite with, &quot;But in my group it's just a rite they get for free.&quot; What you do with your group doesn't matter to Satchel's point, and responding to their point like that doesn't exactly engender better discussions.<br /> <br /> This post also strikes me a kinda blatantly trying to achieve a level of false equivalency on what both sides are saying. The &quot;you're running the game bad-wrong&quot; seems to be pretty much coming from the &quot;make Sacred Hunt innate&quot; crowd, where the &quot;keep it as is&quot; crowd seems to be saying much more, &quot;This way lets people run the game how they want.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T12:35:51-08:00","id":1052113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1051867#post1051867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering I play without houserules. It'd be over 100% more than I normally would communicate actually. You know that you don't need to use houserules to play CofD? :P<br /> <br /> <br /> It doesn't add any Character Choices, it increases the amount of rites werewolf characters starts with. It basically is &quot;treat your werewolf as if he had 2 extra XP, but I'm not letting you pick what that XP goes to&quot;. Werewolves with additional stuff at character creation are already in the rules by giving the werewolf extra XP, while removing the option for characters without the rite which many will probably never want or use in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1052094#post1052094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There might be less defensiveness if you didn't respond to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> who was replying to someone that was saying they made Sacred Hunt not-a-rite with, &quot;But in my group it's just a rite they get for free.&quot; What you do with your group doesn't matter to Satchel's point, and responding to their point like that doesn't exactly engender better discussions.<br /> <br /> This post also strikes me a kinda blatantly trying to achieve a level of false equivalency on what both sides are saying. The &quot;you're running the game bad-wrong&quot; seems to be pretty much coming from the &quot;make Sacred Hunt innate&quot; crowd, where the &quot;keep it as is&quot; crowd seems to be saying much more, &quot;This way lets people run the game how they want.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Milo's posts do come off as judgemental, even with the :P, I was responding to Satchel's idea that the &quot;giving it for free&quot; automatically meant that it wasn't a rite, and the entire presumption surrounding it in the games that were run in that way. <br /> <br /> While I cannot speak for Iry, or Wyrd, my reasons for the innate houserule was to fix an issue that cropped up in my tiny games and I've tried to stress that I don't see it as the new way to swap to overall. I don't see it as a false equivalency but I was defending my choice on it since the last two pages were pretty heavy on the implication that the houserule was a detriment to the game itself, and to player choice.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T13:57:46-08:00","id":1052170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1052094#post1052094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There might be less defensiveness if you didn't respond to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> who was replying to someone that was saying they made Sacred Hunt not-a-rite with, &quot;But in my group it's just a rite they get for free.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I still run it as a rite.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1052094#post1052094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This post also strikes me a kinda blatantly trying to achieve a level of false equivalency on what both sides are saying. The &quot;you're running the game bad-wrong&quot; seems to be pretty much coming from the &quot;make Sacred Hunt innate&quot; crowd, where the &quot;keep it as is&quot; crowd seems to be saying much more, &quot;This way lets people run the game how they want.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some ideas being passed around, and each side is making a pretty civil case for why they think these ideas are good or bad. Not necessarily to convince each other (this is the internet), but with the expectation that people will come in and read both sides of the case and make a decision of their own.<br /> <br /> On one side -- a group of people who are encouraging others to try 2 Ritual Dots AND Sacred Hunt (or providing anecdotal accounts of how it worked out well in their own games).<br /> On the other side -- a group of people who are encouraging others to stick with the status-quo (and there is absolutely nothing wrong with the status-quo).<br /> <br /> Somewhere along the line, the suggestion that <i>'you might have more fun if...'</i> got interpreted as <i>'you're not having fun right now'</i> and <i>'are you telling me what to do?'</i>. But I don't think those negative connotations were ever intended by anybody, and I hope everything can stay awesome and friendly.<br /> <br /> At least, that's my understanding of the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T15:58:10-08:00","id":1052243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1052170#post1052170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one side -- a group of people who are encouraging others to try 2 Ritual Dots AND Sacred Hunt (or providing anecdotal accounts of how it worked out well in their own games).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrdhamster started the thread asking why it was not an innate ability. When told why, he insisted it should be. As anyone is capable of doing what they want at their own table, his repeated insistence that it is wrong, for instance to the writers, implies he wants the game to change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other side -- a group of people who are encouraging others to stick with the status-quo (and there is absolutely nothing wrong with the status-quo). </div> </div> </div>Sort of biased way to put it. The status quo is the game as-is, including the ability to change what you want about it. None of us are demanding you play your game one way or another, only why the setting fits, and if you want to change it at your table, that's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T17:31:41-08:00","id":1052294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1052113#post1052113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Milo's posts do come off as judgemental, even with the :P, I was responding to Satchel's idea that the &quot;giving it for free&quot; automatically meant that it wasn't a rite, and the entire presumption surrounding it in the games that were run in that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't post in absolutes. One post by a poster on the other side of the argument from you coming off as judgemental isn't prove an equivalency here.<br /> <br /> Satchel was posting in response to someone saying that they consider making the Sacred Hunt an innate ability (not just giving it away for free,but Iry's words are, &quot;...making Sacred Hunt an innate ability of Werewolves...&quot;) which is significantly different than giving out more free rites at char-gen.<br /> <br /> Treating &quot;give it for free&quot; and &quot;is an innate ability&quot; as the same thing is very much not engaging with the points people are trying to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see it as a false equivalency but I was defending my choice on it since the last two pages were pretty heavy on the implication that the houserule was a detriment to the game itself, and to player choice. </div> </div> </div>Making a case that a house rule is detrimental to player choice is not an accusation of playing the game wrong. Giving every character something that by default a werewolf doesn't know (such as as Rite) just because they're a werewolf is reducing player choice by definition: they can no longer choose to play a character that doesn't know how to do that thing.<br /> <br /> If you give every character Occult 2, then none of them can make a character that doesn't make sense to have Occult 0 or 1.<br /> <br /> This is a completely designed focused argument, even if it isn't compelling for the needs of your personal table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1052170#post1052170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one side -- a group of people who are encouraging others to try 2 Ritual Dots AND Sacred Hunt (or providing anecdotal accounts of how it worked out well in their own games).<br /> On the other side -- a group of people who are encouraging others to stick with the status-quo (and there is absolutely nothing wrong with the status-quo).</div> </div> </div> </div>This does not feel like an accurate summary of things, since the first side has not solely encouraged that one house rule, and has said much more than just encouraging more starting dots in Rites.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-20T18:03:32-08:00","id":1052309,"title":"","content":"If we are debating the minutia and very specific verbiage being used by one or two posters, we may have gotten away from the spirit of the thread.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1047667-2e-should-not-sacred-hunt-be-inner-ability?p=1052294#post1052294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This does not feel like an accurate summary of things, since the first side has not solely encouraged that one house rule, and has said much more than just encouraging more starting dots in Rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. We <b>are</b> multiple different people saying similar but not actually identical things. Some differing positions were bound to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 02-20-2017, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}